[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_1]
To Develop or Not, That is the Question

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_1_desc]
“Stratusburg Diner Expansion Plan”, “Empire Conscription Office Notice”, “Timbucktu Crystal Mining Plan”, “Cloudsdale Complaints about Stratusburg Muffin Export Quality”... Spitfire was in the office, looking at a stack of reports, irritably swinging her whistle.
As Cloudsdale gradually becoming a welfare society under Duchess Derpy’s leadership, there is no survival pressure, nor space for growth. More ambitious and capable ponies began to look for opportunities in Stratusburg. However, the influx of speculators may not be a good thing for Stratusburg: it is clear to Spitfire, that the most important reason why Stratusburg can survive to this day is not military strength, but economic backwardness: the estimated income that the Empire can obtain from conquering Stratusburg is not enough to make up for the cost of suppression. Once the economy of Stratusburg develops, the benefits of the Empire’s invasion will increase, and the survival of Stratusburg will become more difficult.
Previously, Spitfire’s attitude towards these development proposals was mostly “ignored”, but more and more ponies began to ask, why not approve these harmless proposals? The naive residents of Stratusburg never questioned Spitfire’s leadership, but their questions purely out of curiosity made Spitfire unsure how to answer. Is it a correct choice to stop developing just because of fear of the Empire’s invasion?
Spitfire swung her whistle and began to read these reports one by one.

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_1_o0]
It’s time to make some changes.

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_2]
Stratusburg Diner Expansion Plan

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_2_desc]
The Stratusburg Diner operated by Sky Stinger and Vapor Trail has long been an important part of the night life of Stratusburg residents. Even Spitfire herself will come here every now and then to celebrate with the residents. However, the report submitted by Sky Stinger shows that, as the Diner is trying to keep an affordable price for the residents, the profit of the Diner itself is not too high. Sky Stinger hopes to expand the Diner, not only for Stratusburg, but also for the Greater Cloudsdale area, to increase the profitability of the Diner. In the report, Sky Stinger believed that this is not just for gold coins, but also to increase the popularity of the local brand of Stratusburg.
In addition, Sky Stinger also proposed a more ambitious idea in the report: under Duchess Derpy’s rule, the demand for muffins in Cloudsdale is increasing, and Stratusburg has always maintained a small-scale muffin export to Cloudsdale. Sky Stinger hopes to open a dedicated muffin workshop by expanding the Diner, and he estimates that Duchess Derpy will accept all the muffins exported from Stratusburg like a bottomless pit, which will be a huge business opportunity. Furthermore, the proposal states that the cost of expanding the Diner will be borne by Sky Stinger and Vapor Trail themselves, so Spitfire does not need to worry about it.
Sky Stinger and Vapor Trail are old friends of Spitfire. Back in the Wonderbolts Academy, Spitfire was a coach, and Sky Stinger and Vapor Trail were two of the best students. During training, Sky Stinger often made some reckless decisions, but his flying ability was always enough to get him out of trouble; on the other hoof, Vapor Trail was a very stable pilot, and usually kept a low profile and caution during training. However, this proposal only comes from Sky Stinger, and there is no signature from Vapor Trail, which is worth noting.

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_2_o0]
Help our old friends...?

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_3]
Empire Conscription Office Notice

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_3_desc]
Spitfire didn’t read it carefully, and turned to the next report directly...

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_3_o0]
Next time

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_4]
Timbucktu Crystal Mining Plan

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_4_desc]
This is a proposal from the Cloudsdale Chamber of Commerce. They discovered some shallow crystal mines in the Timbucktu ruins, with huge reserves and high quality, exquisite patterns suitable for making jewelry, and huge potential profits...
However, the greedy capitalists from Cloudsdale do not understand Stratusburg, while Spitfire, who has lived here for several years, has some understanding: Timbucktu was a pegasus city-state in the early days of the two sisters’ regime of Equestria, and had close ties with the then Kingdom of Equesria. Timbucktu was famous for its production of spices (spicy rainbow). The king of Timbucktu accidentally discovered the “cursed crystals”. Soon the crystal jewelry business in Timbucktu boomed, attracting the covetousness of the Changeling Kingdom — Spices meant nothing to the Changelings, but crystals meant wealth. The once worthless city-state of Timbucktu became rich overnight, and disappeared without a trace under the Changelings’ attack.
Therefore, with such ominous signs of the Timbucktu crystals, making jewelry will not have any consumers, let alone huge profits. The Chamber of Commerce naturally does not know this. Even if we use this historical legend to oppose them, they will only regard it as nonsense, or simply let us conceal these stories. Since driven out of Cloudsdale by Duchess Derpy, the Chamber of Commerce has become more and more irresponsible in their actions, and their proposals for Stratusburg have become more and more profit-oriented... Spitfire looked at this proposal, sighed, and put it aside.

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_4_o0]
Reject for now

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_5]
Cloudsdale Complaints about Stratusburg Muffin Export Quality

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_5_desc]
Stratusburg and Cloudsdale have been maintaining a small-scale muffin trade, but recently the residents of Cloudsdale began to complain that the quality of Stratusburg’s muffins has declined, and even food safety incidents have occurred - some Cloudsdale ponies have experienced muffin explosions while refrigerating them!
Spitfire looked at this report and frowned. Muffins? Explosions? Spitfire thought of Sky Stinger’s “Stratusburg Diner Expansion Plan”. Maybe... standardizing the muffin production process and creating a high-quality brand that belongs to Stratusburg now seems to be a rather important development direction.

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_5_o0]
We will look into this

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_6]
The Washouts Tour

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_6_desc]
One afternoon shortly after Jahr Null, Spitfire’s office door was suddenly kicked open, and three pegasi in flight suits and helmets rushed in, followed by a panicked security guard.
“You’d better have something important to say.” Spitfire waved her hoof in disgust, gesturing for the security guard to leave.
The lead pegasus took off his helmet, revealing herself to be Lightning Dust, the captain of the Washouts, with Rolling Thunder and Short Fuse, the core members, on either side. The Washouts are mostly former Wonderbolts Academy students or Wobderbolts who were expelled. And only those expelled for non-ability reasons, such as dangerous flying or not fitting in. They consider themselves the “most talented pegasi” and do not want to be bound by the outdated rules of the Wonderbolts, so they formed the Washouts themselves.

“Happy Jahr Null, Spitfire?” Lightning Dust flew to the desk with a mocking tone, while Rolling Thunder and Short Fuse came to either side of the desk, surrounding Spitfire in the middle. Spitfire made no response, not even taking off her sunglasses.
“Wake up, you old hag! We have the approval of EEMD to hold a touring show celebrating Jahr Null in Stratusburg!” Lightning Dust slammed the table hard, scattering Spitfire’s reports all over the floor. “Or maybe it’s not even a tour. Stratusburg is such a small place, one show is enough.” Rolling Thunder followed with a sneer.

Spitfire swept the already scattered documents off the table, and saw that the table had been dented by Lightning Dust’s slam. She responded directly without any good temper: “The ticket money from your tour must be used to compensate for this table. As for the rest — you pay for the gap yourselves.”
Seeing that Spitfire implied that her show wouldn’t make ticket money, Lightning Dust sneered and turned to leave. Rolling Thunder slapped down the tour poster and two crystal diamonds on the table, looked at Spitfire with seeming jealousy, and then left the office with Short Fuse.

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_6_o0]
How arrogant!

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_7]
The Washouts Profile: Lightning Dust

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_7_desc]
Lightning Dust was a student at the Wonderbolts Academy at the same time as Rainbow Dash. She was expelled by Spitfire for creating a tornado that injured passing ponies during a reckless flight. Since then, she has formed the Washouts. Initially, the Washouts only performed some dangerous stunts. However, as they frequently encountered hazardous situations with props during their performances, Lightning Dust became acquainted with arms dealers who sold gunpowder, cannons, darts, bombs, and flamethrowers. It is difficult to determine precisely when the Washouts began to receive financial support from arms dealers. What is known is that they started using increasingly dangerous props in their performances and promoted them as very awesome and cool props to encourage the audience to buy and imitate. Despite no serious injury incidents occurring thus far, neither the former Empire Royal Commission, the Cloudsdale Chamber of Commerce, nor the current Duchess Derpy or Stratusburg authority fully approve of the Washouts’ behavior.
Today, the backers supporting Lightning Dust may consist of remnants from the Empire and the Chamber of Commerce. As they transitioned from a ruling position to an opposition position, their stance towards the hazardous activities of arms dealers and Lightning Dust shifted rapidly. Many current members of the Chamber of Commerce could potentially be affiliated with arms dealers, viewing Lightning Dust as their most compelling asset. In comparison to the Empire and the Chamber of Commerce, Lightning Dust herself appears to harbor greater ambitions. She is not driven by power or wealth but possesses a fanatical pursuit of the “Extreme talents of a pegasus”. To achieve this, she is willing to perform increasingly dangerous flight stunts hefself, as well as argue with the Empire, the Chamber of Commerce, even subordinates such as Rolling Thunder and Short Fuse, or any other opponents in her way.

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_7_o0]
I’m done

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_7_o1]
Next Page

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_8]
The Washouts Profile: Rolling Thunder

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_8_desc]
Compared to Lightning Dust, the creator of the Washouts, Rolling Thunder is actually the more notorious one. Just like Lightning Dust, Rolling Thunder is not afraid of danger. She enjoys the thrill of dancing on the edge of danger. She is one of the few students in the history of the Wonderbolts Academy who was expelled for “doing barrel rolls through nine hundred million volts of electricity in a raging thunderstorm”. After having such experience, nothingelse in life can be exciting for her anymore. Even joining the Washouts does not bring her enough level of excitement, and she seeks it in other ways.
After the Ultimate Battle, she voluntarily accepted the Royal Commission’s appointment as the temporary head of security in the Greater Cloudsdale area to govern the region. Lightning Dust, dissatisfied with following authority, chose to part ways with Rolling Thunder. Unbeknownst to Lightning Dust, Rolling Thunder was also dissatisfied with obeying authority. Rolling Thunder directly contacted Empress Cozy Glow in private, becoming her eyes and ears, managing the Greater Cloudsdale area, and even making the Royal Commission her surveillance target. The political struggle brought unexpected new excitement to Rolling Thunder: the intoxication of wealth, the desire for increasing power, and the constant crisis of being plotted against, made this daredevil, who pursues excitement regardless of her safety, climb desperately upward the greasy pole as if doing barrel rolls through a thunderstorm.
Until — her recklessly decided to use security forces to suppress the protest at the Weather Factory, which completely ignited the political crisis in Cloudsdale and brought her political career to an end. To quell the escalating turmoil in Cloudsdale, Cozy Glow, who was embroiled in the quagmire of the Crystal War at the time, decided to compromise. Cozy Glow dismissed Rolling Thunder from her position to settle the peace in Cloudsdale. Overnight, Rolling Thunder went from the head of the Greater Cloudsdale District to a nopony, or worse, a despised nopony by the entire city. She had to leave Cloudsdale and return to Lightning Dust’s Washouts, waiting for her next opportunity.
Just like a gambler cannot give up gambling for one lost, two years of political career have planted the desire for power deep in Rolling Thunder’s bones. Evidence suggests that behind the cooperation between Lightning Dust and arms dealers, and more gray transactions, there is Rolling Thunder’s influence. Rolling Thunder is undoubtedly the most favored one by the Empire as well as the most dangerous one among the Washouts.

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_8_o0]
I’m done

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_8_o1]
Next Page

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_8_o2]
Prev Page

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_9]
The Washouts Profile: Short Fuse

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_9_desc]
Unlike the other two ambitious leaders, Short Fuse is relatively mediocre among the Washouts. He was expelled from the Wonderbolts Academy for his inability to control his temper.
Short Fuse only cares about himself. His life consists of three things only: flying, eating, and losing his temper. He is very concerned about his own interests, has little loyalty to his friends, and has never considered losing weight to improve his flying skills.
In the early days of the Washouts, Short Fuse joined the group because he saw Lightning Dust’s performance was very popular and the ticket sales were huge. Later, he followed Rolling Thunder for power and wealth, becoming a member of the Cloudsdale security forces. When Rolling Thunder was promoted to the District head of the Greater Cloudsdale area, Short Fuse took over her position and became the new leader of the Cloudsdale security forces. During his tenure, he did not do anything as bad as Rolling Thunder, but he did not do anything good either. He just took the Empire’s salary and plundered Cloudsdale’s wealth, as the job required. When Rolling Thunder was dismissed, Short Fuse lost everything as well.
Although the Chamber of Commerce and the Washouts have a close relationship now, if the Chamber of Commerce wants to cultivate an insider in the Washouts, Short Fuse is definitely their best choice. Both the Chamber of Commerce and our Stratusburg authorities believe that as long as we give him enough, Short Fuse, as a member of the Washouts, does not mind cooperating with any organization. After all, this has almost happened in history.
The only thing to be careful of, when bargaining with him, is his temper. You may find it hard to believe, but he is really trying to control his temper.

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_9_o0]
I’m done

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_9_o1]
Next Page

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_9_o2]
Prev Page

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_10]
The Washouts Profile: Cloudsdale Chamber of Commerce

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_10_desc]
The Cloudsdale Chamber of Commerce is an organization with a very complex history. The Chamber of Commerce in different periods represents completely different interest groups. The Cloudsdale Chamber of Commerce was established about the time the Royal Commission took over the Greater Cloudsdale area. At that time, most of the members of the Chamber of Commerce were old nobles from Canterlot, representing the interests of the luxury and fashion industry, high-end catering industry, and the interests of the new Empress and the Empire’s new army. As local residents of the Greater Cloudsdale area like Rolling Thunder, gradually gained power, the Chamber of Commerce also added more fresh faces from Cloudsdale, beginning to favor emerging light industries such as the Weather Factory.
The appointment of Feather Flatterfly as the Empire’s Chief Economic Advisor was a major turning point for the Chamber of Commerce. After Rolling Thunder fell from power, Feather Flatterfly was allowed to practice his new economic theories in the Greater Cloudsdale area, starting a year-long era of free trade. During this year, Cloudsdale’s economy developed rapidly, but the lack of regulation allowed profit-seeking businesses like the arms dealers represented by Lightning Dust and the media conglomerates represented by Wind Rider to run rampant in Cloudsdale. Eventually, Derpy’s election ended Feather Flatterfly’s promising experiment. The Chamber of Commerce transformed from an official organization into a private business association. Today, the Cloudsdale Chamber of Commerce is almost almost owned by Wind Rider and is trying to create chaos in various regions such as Stratusburg and Cloudsdale to create opportunities for its own enterprises.

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_10_o0]
I’m done

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_10_o1]
Next Page

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_10_o2]
Prev Page

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_11]
The Washouts Profile: Crystal Diamonds

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_11_desc]
After reading the profile, Spitfire looked at the two crystal diamonds on the table again — the compensation fee left by Rolling Thunder for the table. She picked up one of them and looked at it, watching it sparkle under the light like stars in the night sky.
Wait, this looks like the Timbucktu Crystal! This is weird. Even though the Washouts are engaged in flying stunts and illegal arms trading, they are always on the move and thus unlikely to have any connection to the mining industry. This can only mean that the Timbucktu Crystal has begun to circulate on the market. Faced with high profits, despite not having Spitfire’s approval, the speculative miners have already begun to mine the Timbucktu Crystal...

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_11_o0]
I’m done

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_11_o1]
Prev Page

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_12]
Investigate Muffin Exports

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_12_desc]
During the negotiation process with the buyers in Cloudsdale, they showed to Spitfire, a batch of reserved muffin samples: these muffins look normal, but they will explode when subjected to drastic temperature changes or rapid movement. Cloudsdale side claimed that these muffins were imported from Stratusburg, but Spitfire is very familiar with several restaurants in Stratusburg, and this is definitely not a product of Stratusburg.
Spitfire originally thought that the Cloudsdale representatives would ask Stratusburg to provide complete export records, a list of muffin manufacturers to prove the source of these muffins, but the representatives directly expressed their trust (presumably from the great Duchess Derpy’s instructions), and further proposed the proposal to formalize and scale the import of muffins from Stratusburg.
Spitfire was a little surprised, but then remembered the Stratusburg Diner Expansion Plan from Sky Stinger, which seems like a good opportunity now.

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_12_o0]
Deal...?

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_13]
Cloudsdale-Stratusburg Trade Agreement

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_13_desc]
The Cloudsdale representatives have returned, carrying the will of their Duchess Derpy Hooves: she has learned that many of the residents of Stratusburg are retired Wonderbolts or former students of the Wonderbolts Academy. Therefore, she proposed that Cloudsdale transfer the original site of the Wonderbolts Academy to Stratusburg’s management in exchange for a year’s worth of muffin production. In this way, Cloudsdale does not need to pay any fees, and Stratusburg can obtain the old site of the Wonderbolts Academy.
Since the disbandment of the Wonderbolts, the Wonderbolts Academy has been in a state of disrepair... Until recently, Duchess Derpy Hooves decided to transform this floating island into a muffin paradise. Today, most of the flying training facilities of the Wonderbolts Academy are still preserved, with the addition of some muffin stickers and dolls, and an additional cafeteria for making muffins...

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_13_o0]
Sounds good

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_14]
Empire Conscription Office Notice

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_14_desc]
Due to the lack of response to the last conscription notice, the Empire has once again sent to Stratusburg, a new conscription notice, directly to the trash can of Spitfire’s Office.

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_14_o0]
Next time

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_15]
Empire Conscription Office Notice

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_15_desc]
Due to the lack of response to the last conscription notice, the Empire has once again sent to Stratusburg, a new conscription notice, directly to the trash can of Spitfire’s Office.

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_15_o0]
Next time

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_16]
Empire Conscription Office Notice

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_16_desc]
Due to the lack of response to the last conscription notice, the Empire has once again sent to Stratusburg, a new conscription notice, directly to Spitfire’s Office — but this time, Spitfire thought about it and picked up the conscription notice... to use it as a table mat to prevent the lunch crumbs from messing up the table.

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_16_o0]
Next time

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_17]
Vapor Trail’s Proposal

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_17_desc]
Before Vapor Trail could go to look for Sky Stinger, Sky Stinger had already flown into Spitfire’s office.
“If I’m not mistaken, you’re here for Sky Stinger’s expansion plan. How’s he been lately?” Spitfire took off her sunglasses and looked at Vapor Trail.
“He... he... he’s doing fine.” Vapor Trail seemed a little hesitant, then immediately turned the topic to business: “Um, about Sky Stinger’s expansion plan... Actually, I’ve concealed some things from him.”
Spitfire frowned, indicating Vapor Trail to continue.
“We proposed that the cost of expanding the diner be borne by ourselves in the proposal... But we don’t have enough funds.” Vapor Trail’s voice grew smaller and smaller, and she seemed very worried about Spitfire’s reaction. “I’m confident in the profits of expanding the diner, so I don’t want to just dampen Sky Stinger’s enthusiasm because we don’t have the startup capital... So, I want to ask for your help. Can I... Can I apply for a loan from Stratusburg?”

“Well, how much do you need?” Spitfire looked at Vapor Trail and asked.
“Preliminary estimates... If we want to support exporting muffins to Cloudsdale on a large scale, we need an upstream supply chain, the construction of a cold storage warehouse, and a larger kitchen...” Vapor Trail pondered, completely lost in her own thoughts.

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_17_o0]
We’ll consider it

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_18]
Cloudsdale-Stratusburg Trade Agreement

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_18_desc]
After our negotiations with Stratusburg, they have agreed to exchange our old Wonderbolts Academy site for a year’s worth of free muffin production. This way, we can not only save a lot of money, but also make better use of the old Wonderbolts Academy site.
Since the disbandment of the Wonderbolts, the Wonderbolts Academy has been in a state of disrepair... Until recently, this floating island was transformed into a muffin paradise. Today, most of the flying training facilities of the Wonderbolts Academy are still preserved, with the addition of some muffin stickers and dolls, and an additional cafeteria for making muffins...

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_18_o0]
Sounds good

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_18_o1]
Well, let’s not do that

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_19]
Backstage Pass · I

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_19_desc]
On the day of the Washouts’ tour, Spitfire arrived at the venue with a group of Stratusburg leaders, sitting in the front row of the audience.
On the surface, Spitfire, as the appointed lord of the autonomous territory of the Empire, must actively attend the tour under the name of “Celebrating Jahr Null”; in fact, Spitfire came to watch the show. As expected by Spitfire, the residents of Stratusburg remained united: except for the members brought by Spitfire, no resident of Stratusburg attended the show —— which means that Lightning Dust and the others probably couldn’t get any ticket money, let alone recover the cost of the performance venue they built at their own expense.

As the green torches were suddenly ignited, the Washouts’ performance began. Lightning Dust appeared in the center of the stage with Rolling Thunder and Short Fuse. Lightning Dust seemed not surprised by the empty seats, but instead smiled and bowed to Spitfire’s crowd in the front row, and then began their stunt performance in the almost empty audience seats.
Between the fire rings, electric saws, fireworks, and poison fog, Lightning Dust and Rolling Thunder flew and rolled, while Short Fuse threw darts and exploding muffins at them. For them, this was an exciting moment, not because of the performance —— but because of the two hoofguns hidden behind the green torch at the finish line.

As lightning Dust flew, she occasionally glanced at Spitfire with the corner of her eye: she saw Spitfire still sitting there watching the show, seemingly enjoying the performance. “At the last moment of your life, enjoy the heroic posture of the students you expelled. These performances will be standards you will never reach in your remaining life.” Lightning Dust thought with joy in her heart, flying with Rolling Thunder towards the green torch fire at the end.

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_19_o0]
The final sprint comes

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_20]
Backstage Pass · II

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_20_desc]
“Bang!”
With a sharp, deafening crack, the green flames of the arena die out. Lightning Dust and Rolling Thunder come to a stop at the finish line, their performance cut short.
“What’s going on?” Short Fuse shouts. He looks towards Lightning Dust and Rolling Thunder at the finish line, who haven’t had a chance to pull out their hoofguns.

The loud noise doesn’t come from the hoofguns, but from backstage... It turns out that long before the show began, Spitfire had secretly arranged for a group of Stratusburg police to raid the Washouts’ backstage. There, they found various dangerous props, some exploding muffins, many Timbucktu crystal jewelry, and records of the Washouts’ and the Empire’s connections.

The exploding muffins match the samples from Cloudsdale, which means that the Washouts are the culprits behind the Cloudsdale muffin explosion incident. Although no casualties were caused, this is not enough to put them in prison, but at least there is enough reason to drive them out of Stratusburg.

The Timbucktu crystal jewelry is Rolling Thunder’s own collection, which seems to be a legal purchase and shows no signs of resale. Rolling Thunder has almost all of her savings exchanged for these jewelry, which doesn’t seem to fit the image of a Washout seeking excitement regardless of material possessions. But in any case, this violates Spitfire’s ban on the sale of Timbucktu crystal, so Spitfire chooses to confiscate these jewelry.

And the Washouts’ connection to the Empire shows... that unidentified agents of the Empire have entered Stratusburg.

As Lightning Dust and the other Washouts are taken away by the Stratusburg police, Lightning Dust and Spitfire’s eyes meet again. This time, neither side speaks, but both laugh inside. It seems that neither of them realized the other’s secret.

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_20_o0]
Remarkable Performance

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_21]
Control Group

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_21_desc]
“We did it!”
The researchers in the new weather lab cheered excitedly as they looked at the data on the paper tape — the dots burned with charcoal on the paper tape was black, but to them it was as bright and shining as the sun — those are the temperature measurement data transmitted from the weather factory. The celebration had not yet ended, and a more enthusiastic noise erupted in the lab: at the success of the experiment, a pony in the research group confessed to his colleague whom he had secretly admired for a long time.

“Just like our experiment, as long as we are together, we can create miracles.”
He said, holding up a bouquet of flowers. Behind them, the black dots on the paper tape were still rolling, and the paper tape transcriber wrote +1.8 on the glass board in the lab with charcoal — the temperature in the weather factory area had risen by 1.8 degrees since their new production line started. Years ago, as the activities of the Windigo intensified and the Wonderbolts disbanded, the production capacity of the weather factory was no longer sufficient to maintain warmth; the newly established Canterlot regime was also at war with the northern empire of ice and snow. Therefore, Cozy Glow ordered the merger of the weather factory and the weather lab, and established the Equestria Meteorological Bureau to cooperate in research on how to raise the temperature. However, shortly after the establishment of the Meteorological Bureau, the riot of workponies at the weather factory almost completely destroyed the collaboration project, leaving the weather lab in ruins. It was not until Spitfire took office, rebuilt the weather lab, that the communication and research between the two sides slowly resumed.

“I want our love to be as warm and passionate as the new production line; I want our life to be better and better like the dots on the paper tape! Will you... be my girlfriend?” The pony said, handing over the flowers; his lover opposite him was already in tears. Behind them, the transcriber wrote down the number +3.3.

“I do!”
At this moment, even the transcriber who had been sticking to his duties could not help but be emotional when he saw this scene. He grabbed the paper tape and began to transmit the coded information to the weather factory: “A pony in the weather lab just confessed!~” After sending the message, the transcriber looked at the still jumping paper tape, turned around and wrote down the number +5.6 on the glass board. Soon, the paper tape stopped jumping, and then the weather factory began to transmit coded information. It must be their blessing to the couple! The transcriber took down the new paper tape and began to transcribe the information on the black dots.

“Weather factory, we wish you — uh... your giraffe’s mane will not transport pink donuts... Huh?” The transcriber looked at the information on the paper tape, confused. Then he suddenly realized that the paper tape was upside down! He quickly turned the paper tape over and transcribed it again, this time the information on the paper tape was a vulgar curse.

Tonight at the weather factory, the workponies shivered in the cold wind that was 7 degrees lower than before.

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_21_o0]
Refrigerator anecdote — a scientist couple

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_22]
Angel Investor · I

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_22_desc]
Inside Spitfire’s office, the black coffee in the gilt-edged enamel cup is still steaming.

Spitfire is not an appreciator of this kind of coffee, not to mention this cup of Starswirl coffee worth three gold coins, like a black vortex, used up the last half jar of sugar of her. Currently, Cloudsdale is financially strained, with expenses for meteorological research, small diner expansions, and the reconstruction of the Wonderbolts Academy, all of which are heavy burdens that the small Cloudsdale cannot afford. Spitfire certainly cannot afford the extra expense to enjoy luxurious coffee. No, this cup of coffee is prepared for a special guest, a guest who can solve all the aforementioned problems.

Soon, a female pegasus in a black suit, followed by two bodyguards, walked in. Laurette Dove, the heir of the Dove family. Miss Laurette is not considered wealthy compared to some members of the Cloudsdale Chamber of Commerce. However, Miss Laurette is the most generous among the rich — perhaps only second to Rarity back then. She never minds investing the family’s assets into projects that do not see any short-term returns. In fact, during Princess Celestia’s reign, Laurette provided a lot of free funding for the Wonderbolt team; some ponies in the Chamber of Commerce, who are now far wealthier than Laurette, got their start-up capital from her back then. In recent years, when the subsidies from the Empire were insufficient to cover expenses, Laurette also generously provided low-interest loans to help Cloudsdale through tough times; during the famine, Miss Laurette would also buy food with her own money to distribute to the poor.

Therefore, Spitfire is very confident that Laurette will offer help to the government to solve the financial difficulty again — until Miss Laurette sat down and pushed the coffee in front of her aside.

Miss Laurette stared at the gold-edged plaque with her name at the top of the list of “sponsors of the past Equestria Games” on the wall, for a long long time before speaking, still with hesitation in her voice.

“Emm... I have to say, the diner expansion plan you proposed is very attractive,”

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_22_o0]
“But...?”

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_23]
Angel Investor · II

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_23_desc]
“Governer Spitfire, I hope you can understand...” As Laurette explained, Spitfire learned that due to Laurette’s long-term charitable investments, the Do family’s business in the west had hardly grown, and even shrunk. Therefore, Laurette could no longer provide large sums of money as she used to. She sought help from those “business partners” she had supported in the past, only to find that those savvy businessponies had long taken her generosity for granted, and some were even dissatisfied with her amount of support.

However, Laurette also proposed her solution: Laurette had long sponsored the Wonderbolt team, and her company had arranged jobs for many retired Wonderbolt members. Wind Rider, who was kicked out of the Wonderbolt team due to a grudge with Rainbow Dash, had grown into a wealthy entertainment industry businessman with Laurette’s support. If Laurette introduced Wind Rider to invest in Stratusburg’s government, Wind Rider would likely accept. However, unlike Laurette’s generosity, for Wind Rider, Stratusburg might need to offer higher returns... such as the rights to mine crystals in Timbucktu and a license for arms smuggling...

“We don’t feel too comfortable dealing with those speculators...” Spitfire said.

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_23_o0]
“Of course, not including you, I mean Wind Rider.”

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_23_o1]
“But sometimes that’s what we have to do.”

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_23_TOOLTIP]
§CWind Rider§! will obtain exclusive mining rights in Timbucktu.

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_23_TRIGGER_TOOLTIP]
§CWind Rider§! will obtain exclusive mining rights in Timbucktu, and Stratusburg will no longer levy high taxes.

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_24]
Angel Investor · III

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_24_desc]
“That nerd next to Cozy Glow?” Spitfire took off her sunglasses and glanced at Miss Laurette, surprised and almost wanting to blow her instructor whistle.

After Spitfire rejected Laurette’s proposal to cooperate with Wind Rider, the next on the list of benefactors was Feather Flatterfly — the current Chief Economic Advisor of the Empire, and the commander of the Cloudsdale FTZ project. Spitfire still remained wary of this pony who had become a high-ranking member of the Empire, as well as the most capable economic aide in the service of Cozy Glow and Fancy Pants. However, judging from the increasingly crazy economic policies of the Empire: Feather Flatterfly, who is now inside the political center Canterlot, has long been marginalized by the civil group and secret police. His liberal economic theory has also been thrown aside.

Miss Laurette said that when she communicated with Feather Flatterfly in Canterlot yesterday, he expressed his intention to resign and return to Stratusburg. Feather Flatterfly hoped to re-implement his theory and continue the economic reform experiment that was interrupted by Duchess Derpy Hooves. An autonomous dominion without interference from the Empire officials was the best experimental field. However, at the same time, he also understood that the nobles in the Empire did not want to see this experiment succeed, and would do everything they could to obstruct Feather Flatterfly’s plan. This forced Feather Flatterfly to stay in Canterlot, tightly holding onto the little power of the Chief Advisor he had left. Therefore, Miss Laurette proposed that Feather Flatterfly would provide funds to help the Stratusburg government solve its financial problems: the condition was that Stratusburg would accept Feather Flatterfly’s economic theory for reform, allowing Feather Flatterfly to create a successful experimental zone to showcase to Empress Cozy Glow.

“So, we’re building diner in Stratusburg just to make Feather Flatterfly help Cozy Glow get richer?” Spitfire asked back, her voice tinged with sarcasm.
“But, once Feather Flatterfly’s theory succeeds, not only will Cozy Glow get richer, but the entire Empire’s economy will benefit. Every pony, ordinary ponies, including you and me and Stratusburg, will benefit.” Laurette said.

“I’m still skeptical,” listening to Laurette’s somewhat unusually enthusiastic recommendation, Spitfire disdainfully put on her sunglasses.

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_24_o0]
“But, sometimes that’s what we have to do.”

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_24_o1]
“I’d rather choose Wind Rider than the Empire.”

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_24_TOOLTIP]
§RThe Cloudsdale government will no longer intervene in the economy.§!

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_24_TRIGGER_TOOLTIP]
§RBecause of the cooperation with Feather Flatterfly, the Cloudsdale government will no longer intervene in the economy.§!

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_26]
New Employee · I

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_26_desc]
“Bang!”

As Spitfire was listening to the reports made by Sky Stinger and Vapor Trail on the monthly muffin production capacity of the small diner, the door to her office was suddenly kicked open with a loud bang, and in came the red-coated Short Fuse. Before Sky Stinger even had time to react, Vapor Trail had already hidden behind her chair in fear, while Spitfire instinctively reached into her drawer for a hoofgun. However, she noticed that Short Fuse, although looking extremely angry, was not carrying any weapons.

“Two lunatics!” Short Fuse cursed angrily. “Lightning Dust and Rolling Thunder have made a fortune! And what did I get? I! GOT! NOTHING!”
As Short Fuse was yelling, he saw the lunchboxes on Spitfire’s desk. Before Vapor Trail could even say anything, Short Fuse had already opened the lunchbox and swallowed the sandwich inside in one gulp. Vapor Trail could only shrink back behind her chair and watch as the lunch she had made for Sky Stinger was eaten by Short Fuse.

Short Fuse had joined the Washouts not to pursue the same extremes or excitement as Lightning Dust and Rolling Thunder, but simply to earn more ticket money and buy more delicious food. However, since the touring performances had stopped after Lightning Dust and Rolling Thunder were imprisoned, Short Fuse and his fellow Washouts had lost their source of income. Short Fuse had originally hoped that his leaders would be released from prison soon, but when he began to take care of the affairs, he discovered that his leaders had their secret treasure pots that he had never known about — Lightning Dust made a fortune through arms dealing, while Rolling Thunder made a fortune through gambling and hoarding Timbucktu crystals. “They both made a fortune!” Short Fuse gritted his teeth once again. “And they DON’T EVEN WANT TO BUY A FEW MORE SANDWICHES! They’d rather squander their money on dangerous equipment, training grounds, and flight performances than BUY A FEW MORE SANDWICHES!”

Spitfire, Sky Stinger, and Vapor Trail looked at each other, not knowing how to respond to this “defector” from the enemy team. Would a Washout really betray his leader just because of a little unfair distribution of loot? Vapor Trail secretly leaned towards Spitfire, tugging at her clothes with her wings and conveying her suspicions with her eyes, while Spitfire, who had dealt with the Washouts for quite some time, knew that Short Fuse was indeed a fool, probably. Spitfire gestured for Sky Stinger to take out his notebook: regardless of Short Fuse’s motives, the first thing to do was to write down his testimony.

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_26_o0]
“Tell us more about the arms dealing and gambling?”

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_27]
New Employee · II

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_27_desc]
“... And that’s not all. Last year, they suddenly told me, ‘The Washouts are planning something big’，” Short Fuse continued eating the sandwich Vapor Trail had just brought back from outside. His mouth was full but that did not stop him from complaining, “I thought they were going to do some big performance, but they said they were going to open a muffin factory. I went to help them, but after two days of making muffins, they kicked me out!”
Hearing this, Vapor Trail couldn’t help but laugh. Since last year, the Washouts had been producing cupcake explosives. Selling military-grade explosives as muffins was indeed a good idea: not only could they fool the police, but sometimes they could even fool the customers and the Washouts’ own employees — like Short Fuse.

At this point, Short Fuse suddenly paused. Seeing the chart in the office, which was coincidentally the muffin production chart of the small diner, his eyes lit up. “OH! THAT’S WHY! So you just caught them to take over their muffin business! No wonder! I heard you monopolized all the orders in Cloudsdale! ALL! THE! MUFFIN! ORDERS!” Short Fuse became more and more excited as he spoke, and the vegetable, bread and tomato residue in his mouth flew everywhere, forcing Vapor Trail to hide behind Sky Stinger again.
“I gave you so much information about your opponents, and I saw your plan. Now, I should get a share of the muffin business, RIGHT!?” Short Fuse requested in a tone that was not at all like a request.

And that’s it. Short Fuse became the new employee of the Stratusburg small diner, Sky Stinger became Short Fuse’s new employee training supervisor, Vapor Trail carefully organized Short Fuse’s testimony, and Spitfire prepared to post the wanted posters for the arrest of Lightning Dust and Rolling Thunder. Everypony had their own business to attend to. However, the small diner would not make any profit in the first year, as all the products were sent to Cloudsdale for free. So the employees could only receive the meager subsidy provided by the Cloudsdale government, which is a fact that Spitfire never dared to tell Short Fuse.

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_27_o0]
That’s so funny

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_28]
Harmonism Education

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_28_desc]
In the afternoon of the Stratusburg Diner, Short Fuse was lying on the bench in the corner, snoring, with an opened book — Friendship Diary: Annotated Edition — on him, and a bottle of seemingly red wine beside him.

After finishing the lunch business and cleaning up the kitchen with Vapor Trail, Sky Stinger walked towards Short Fuse and poked him with the tip of his wing. The red pegasus, who was startled awake, almost rolled off the bench. The Friendship Diary also fell to the ground, only flipping to the third page, with another book sandwiched inside, displaying illustrations of poker cards and magic props.

“What are you actually reading instead of friendship materials?” Sky Stinger raised an eyebrow, flipping the book to the title page with his wing. The golden letters of “20 Magic Tricks in Daily Life Taught by the Great and Powerful Trixie” sparkled under the sunlight. “Magic tricks? You’d rather learn this than friendship?”

Short Fuse, who was still half-asleep, was about to get angry, but he took a deep breath instead. “That’s not true! Isn’t reading Friendship Diary supposed to help me control my temper? I think the methods of managing emotions in Magic Tricks are more practical!”

Seeing that Short Fuse controlled his temper, Sky Stinger seemed a bit surprised, but he still advised like a real teacher, “Not entirely. Harmonism also includes many other aspects, such as tolerance, understanding, respect, helping friends... These are all things you need to learn.” Sky Stinger looked at Short Fuse, who seemed a bit dissatisfied but didn’t lose his temper. Was it for money? Or did his temper really improve?

“I understand the principles, but why do I have to read this old Friendship Diary? Canterlot has already published a new version of Harmonism, right? Why not learn the new one?” Short Fuse grumbled impatiently. Seeing Sky Stinger’s face getting more and more gloomy, he quickly added, “...em... I mean, if you just want me to learn the old one, I’ll just do it them. I didn’t refuse... Maybe you are the one who really should read Magic Tricks to control your temper!” Then he left the diner with his Friendship Diary, Magic Tricks, and red wine, leaving Sky Stinger at a loss for words.

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_28_o0]
He’s learning anyway

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_29]
The Model Student

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_29_desc]
Months have passed, and Short Fuse is like a completely different pony now. Just this afternoon, while Vapor Trail was calculating the restaurant’s income and expenses, she accidentally knocked Short Fuse into a large barrel of muffin syrup. Vapor Trail was terrified and kept apologizing to Short Fuse who was covered in syrup, but he just climbed out of the barrel and left without saying a word.
Short Fuse is no longer hot-tempered. The restaurant staff were surprised by this change. Vapor Trail is preparing to award Short Fuse the Model Student medal, while Sky Stinger is reporting Short Fuse’s change to Spitfire. “This is a successful showcase of Harmonism education!” Sky Stinger wrote in the report. However, Sky Stinger’s task is not yet complete: some employees have reported that Short Fuse hasn’t been taking the Harmonism textbooks seriously, and his recent spirit doesn’t seem to be good. He appears dull and lethargic, and often feels tired. Sky Stinger remembered that Short Fuse always brought a bottle of wine whenever they talked, and couldn’t help but worry that Short Fuse might have developed a drinking problem, or even worse, might have come into contact with the addictive “Pegasus Joy Juice”.
In any case, Short Fuse’s positive change is obvious, and he just needs to pass one final test to graduate as a model student — Is he still greedy for money now? Next, Spitfire will tell Short Fuse that he won’t be getting a bonus this year because the muffin orders from the first year was unpaid, and see how he reacts (in fact, Spitfire and Sky Stinger have already prepared a generous bonus for Short Fuse out of their own pockets).

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_29_o0]
Interesting

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_30]
Frugal Luxury · I

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_30_desc]
On the west side of the Weather Factory, a silver-plated and diamond-studded palanquin slowly stopped, followed by a bodyguard team of only two ponies that was completely inconsistent with the luxury. Feather Flatterfly, dressed in high-end suits, walked out of the palanquin carefully. Just like his palanquin, he was a contradictory hybrid of both flaunting luxury and introverted restraint.
Miss Laurette had been waiting here for a long time, and soon she approached Flatterfly, the Empire’s Chief Economic Advisor, to introduce the surrounding situation. When Miss Laurette saw Flatterfly’s palanquin, she cleverly said nothing, instead of praising it — because Miss Laurette knew that Flatterfly actually hated this palanquin. Flatterfly, who was raised in a commoner family, couldn’t stand the extravagance of the nobles and bureaucrats in Canterlot. However, indulging himself in luxury was the only way to connect with them, and without it, those bureaucrats would sabotage all his economic policies and reform decisions. Therefore, he had to choose a palanquin that looked as luxurious as possible, yet as simple and cheap as possible.
This field trip to the Weather Factory was taken advantage of the opportunity to visit Cloudsdale, and Flatterfly secretly came here without Canterlot’s orders. Those fat and short-sighted ponies in Canterlot only coveted Cloudsdale, wanting to turn the seemingly endless Muffin Factory under Derpy’s management into a producer of luxury goods and weapons for the Empire. Only Flatterfly, who saw the true value of Cloudsdale, realized that the abandoned Meteorological Bureau held the control of the world’s weather. Only by dispersing the Windigos could the entire Equestria Empire achieve long-term prosperity, and only with warmer soil could it support the high expenses of the Empress and those corrupt bureaucrats. Unlike Cloudsdale, which is governed by Derpy who is completely not communicatable, Stratusburg is where Flatterfly hopes to achieve his goal. He hopes to practice his economic theories in the Stratusburg Autonomous Region, prove his worth to Canterlot, and ultimately persuade the Empress to increase investment in the Meteorological Bureau and start a national economic reform...

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_30_o0]
It seems that the Weather Factory is doing well without the Empire’s management

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_31]
Frugal Luxury · II

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_31_desc]
... Even though Flatterfly no longer deals with grassroots affairs, he never forgets his fear back then...
It was still the era of Princess Celestia. Flatterfly, who graduated from the Royal Academy of Celestia with the highest score in economics, entered the palace as an intern under Fancy Pants’s command. However, his first task in the palace almost ended Flatterfly’s political career: the logistics of the Summer Sun Setback was a mess. Fortunately, during that difficult time, Cozy Glow — who was still a foal and not yet the Empress — discovered his talent and calmed him down when he was on the verge of collapse. With the help of M6, Flatterfly narrowly survived that night.
Since then, Flatterfly has deeply realized a truth: plans can never keep up with changes. No pony has the ability to predict the future, not even the Princess Twilight Sparkle who crazed about making plans. When he re-examined the economic theories of the old nobles of the Royal Academy from the perspective of “masterly inactivity”, he found a new possibility: ponies have the ability to spontaneously organize economic activities — just like when one pony starts singing, other ponies will follow. Perhaps, ponies do not need economists, do not need him and bureaucrats like Fancy Pants, and do not even need a princess. Only by returning everything to the ponies and letting them produce, sell, and buy freely, can Flatterfly no longer have to recall the headache he had as a coordinator that night.
However, it was not until the moment when Flatterfly’s plan was placed on the desk of Empress Cozy Glow that Flatterfly realized, the Friendship Empress who helped him when he was most desperate, seemed not always so friendly...

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_31_o0]
Alas...

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_32]
The Conclave · I

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_32_desc]
When Sky Stinger and Vapor Trail pushed open the door to Spitfire’s office, they found her bidding farewell to the visibly distressed Miss Laurette. “We’ll discuss this another time, Miss Laurette.” Spitfire reassured her.
As Miss Laurette exited with her head lowered, she accidentally bumped into Sky Stinger, knocking his backpack to the ground. Files scattered everywhere — documents about Stratusburg, some detailing restaurant finances, others tracking the post-retirement developments of former Wonderbolts, a few stamped with bold “TOP SECRET” markings... and amidst them, Sky Stinger’s idle doodles. Perhaps from reading too many Friendship Journals, his crude sketches depicted him wielding the Elements of Harmony, firing rainbow lasers like Twilight Sparkle once did. Even the previously gloomy Miss Laurette couldn’t help but chuckle. Flustered, Sky Stinger hastily blocked the papers, muttering something about “classified materials, no peeking!”
Vapor Trail, however, didn’t laugh. She knew the gravity of today’s discussion that is about to happen — about the very “TOP SECRET” documents now on the floor. Sky Stinger had long planned this: while the Empire was preoccupied with eastern affairs, Stratusburg would declare independence, raise the banner of Harmonism, and challenge the Empire, reigniting the glory of harmony alongside their eastern allies.

As a former participant in the Free Cloudsdale Movement, now leader of the Free Stratusburg Movement and Governer of the Stratusburg Dominion, Spitfire understood the fragility of their city. Against the Empire, independence might seem like a suicidal farce. Yet, gazing at the newly restored Wonderbolts Academy, she couldn’t help but wonder if past failures had shackled herself. These two young faces in front of her — Sky Stinger and Vapor Trail — had achieved what she couldn’t in years. They reopened the academy, transformed Stratusburg’s economy from relying on imperial subsidies to self-sufficiency driven by cuisine and crystal industries...

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_32_o0]
Maybe it’s not a bad idea to listen to Sky Stinger’s plan...

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_33]
The Conclave · II

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_33_desc]
Weather Factory, Rainbow Factory, and the Wonderbolts Academy — these three locations have the highest number of retired Wonderbolts working there, and are now nominally under the jurisdiction of Sire’s Hollow, Cloudsdale, and Stratusburg separately. Sky Stinger proposed that even if Stratusburg cannot openly challenge the Empire at this time, dealing with the militia along the borders of Cloudsdale and Sire’s Hollow would be an easy task. If Stratusburg could seize these areas in a surprise attack, the Empire would learn of it too late to react. Besides, with the Empire’s forces tied up on the eastern front, there’s no reason they would send troops to intervene in these “disputes between internal districts”. Meanwhile, Stratusburg could take this opportunity to completely eliminate the Washouts entrenched in the Unicorn Mountain Range and secure the crystal mining areas in Timbucktu.
Sky Stinger then continued, suggesting that if Stratusburg successfully took control of these three regions, we would have a real chance to gather nearly all former Wonderbolt members and rebuild an unmatched aerial force across all of Equestria. The Wonderbolts would finally return to the sky! After that, Sky Stinger and Vapor Trail presented some detailed analyses on the Empire’s troop deployments, the militia forces along the borders, and the possible reactions from Canterlot... They also sought opinions from other aspects of Stratusburg, and Wind Rider agreed enthusiastically, expressing willingness to fund and recruit members for the plan — not because of his past as a Wonderbolt, but simply because he wanted to expand the business of the Timbucktu Crystal Industry into the Empire’s territory.
In the end, this plan was named “Return to the Sky”, and the Wonderbolts would soon begin to gather to support its implementation.

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_33_o0]
Mission Start

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_34]
Shiny Blue Muffin

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_34_desc]
Stratusburg Diner’s new product: Shiny Blue Muffin!

§g“What’s the glowing material? Are you sure it’s edible?”§!

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_34_o0]
Okay

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_35]
Flying Muffin

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_35_desc]
Stratusburg Diner’s new product: Shiny Muffin!

§g“Yes, the wings are delicious.”§!

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_35_o0]
Okay

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_36]
Black Muffin Deluxe

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_36_desc]
Stratusburg Diner’s new product: Black Muffin Deluxe!

§g“Emm... Are you sure this isn’t burnt?”§!

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_36_o0]
Okay

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_37]
Crystal Muffin

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_37_desc]
Stratusburg Diner’s new product: Crystal Muffin!

§g“Oh come on, is this ever going to end? Is this even edible?”§!

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_37_o0]
Okay

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_38]
Apple Pie

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_38_desc]
Stratusburg Diner’s new product: Apple Pie!

§g“It is said that a pony couldn’t stand eating muffins every day, voluntarily paid for the ingredients of apple pie and gifted them to the diner...”§!

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_38_o0]
Okay

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_39]
Return to the Sky

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_39_desc]
As the reborn Wonderbolts streaked across Stratusburg’s skyline, the city held its breath. Their yellow-and-blue forms tore through the clouds, contrails painting the sunset — as if the Elements had never shattered, as if the war had never been.
Spitfire led with wings moving like clockwork. Behind her, Vapor Trail and Sky Stinger followed in flawless formation, their wake weaving an invisible stairway to the heavens.
“Now!” As they approached Canterlot, Spitfire shouted. The three Wonderbolts accelerated, the clouds collapsing and evaporating in their shockwave, and finally —

BOOM!
The sonic rainboom detonated over Canterlot, triple the radius of Rainbow Dash’s legendary blast. Its shockwave scoured the land, dissolving the Windigos’ remnants, freezing enslaved ponies mid-labor. Their manes lifted without wind, eyes glowing with unnatural light.
Pamphlets rained down.
Nobles picked one up with shaking hooves.
Secret police officers dropped their weapon.
On the palace balcony, Cozy Glow shredded a page — only to hear her own voice scream:
“CONSOLE IS MAGIC!”

— Then, the world glitched.
The sky flickered like a broken screen. Spitfire’s wings froze mid-dive. Sky Stinger’s grin pixelated into jagged cubes. A soft sigh echoed from the horizon, it was Vapor Trail, “... even the console found it too absurd.”

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_39_o0]
The End

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_40]
The Sun Rises

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_40_desc]
Today was Stratusburg’s momentous day. In the dim pre-dawn light, the city hall meeting room already teemed with pegasi: Sky Stinger, Harmonism apprentice and founder of Stratusburg Diner; Vapor Trail, Stratusburg government consultant and leader of the Sepal Militia; Wind Rider, chairpony of the Cloudsdale Chamber of Commerce; along with former Wonderbolt members and trainees.
Sky Stinger had prepared his speech, even triple-checked for absent-minded doodles on the reverse side of the speech draft. Vapor Trail sat impassively, her gaze alternating between Sky Stinger and the window’s vista, her thoughts a mystery to all. Wind Rider sat at the table, sipping his Starswirl coffee, lost in his own world, seemingly oblivious to the gathering tension in the room.
...
As the first rays of sunlight finally pierced through the gaps in the clouds from below, dyeing the meeting room’s ceiling in hues of orange and red, Sky Stinger had already unfolded his speech draft for the fifth time. The edges of the thin cloud-paper were warped from sweat. Vapor Trail abruptly rose and walked to the window, her reflection in the cloud-glass revealing faint flickers of light in her pupils — the eastern clouds now bled a rusty hue.
Outside the city hall, a group of young Wonderbolt recruits stood fully armored in their red-and-blue uniforms, ready to take flight, though the prolonged wait had visibly frayed their composure. Wind Rider stirred the coffee grounds at the bottom of his cup with a spoon, as if searching for some hidden meaning, before giving up with a yawn. When the spoon clinked against the porcelain, the only sound left in the room was the relentless crinkling of Sky Stinger’s speech draft.
...
By the time the blinding-white sunlight fully breached the cloud layer, the meeting room door finally swung open. But instead of Spitfire, an ashen-faced Sepal Militia member stumbled in.
“Has the Empire attacked?” Wind Rider blurted, tossing his coffee cup aside and surging forward, already poised to bolt from the room. Sky Stinger jerked his head up, speech forgotten, while Vapor Trail whipped around from the window.
“It’s... Governer Spitfire...” The militia member’s wings trembled, melted ice crystals mingling with blood dripping onto the floor. “We found her collapsed behind the apple pie stand behind the diner... She’s covered in blood when we found her...”

The sun now loomed fully above the clouds, its crimson dawn spilling mercilessly through the window. The light hung like a gaze, unblinking and accusatory, piercing straight into the heart of the room.

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_40_o0]
What?!

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_41]
Stratusburg Shooting Incident

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_41_desc]
The Stratusburg Shooting Incident finally thrust this otherwise unremarkable town into the headlines: last night, the governer of the Stratusburg Dominion was shot at the Stratusburg Diner by an unidentified assailant. She has since been rushed to Stratusburg Hospital for emergency treatment and remains in critical condition.
Empress Cozy Glow was quick to address the incident, vehemently condemning this “brazen attack on an imperial civil servant” and announcing plans to deploy Ministry of Order and Ministry of Friendship investigators to assist the local government. However, the acting governer Sky Stinger, Spitfire’s apprentice, declined the Empire’s assistance, asserting that Stratusburg would conduct its own investigation.

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_41_o0]
Okey

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_41_o1]
Maybe it was the Empire’s doing

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_42]
After the Gunshot

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_42_desc]
Not long after, the Stratusburg police identified the perpetrator through the traces at the scene: an abandoned hoofgun, bloodstains, some glass shards, and a pool of pink liquid that seemed to have mixed with some blood at the apple pie stand where Spitfire was attacked. The hoofgun belonged to Spitfire herself, but the broken glass bottle didn’t belong to her; it seems like — Sky Stinger immediately recalled that this was Short Fuse’s bottle.
The remaining pink liquid was sent for testing, and Sky Stinger immediately issued a wanted notice for Short Fuse throughout Stratusburg. But what puzzled Sky Stinger was, why?
Was it a failure of Harmonism education? Or was it just Short Fuse’s momentary impulse? Or did he really have a drinking problem or even an abuse issue with “Pegasus Joy Juice”? Or was it possible... that he was a rat planted by the Washouts from the very beginning?

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_42_o0]
Okey

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_43]
To Come out on Top

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_43_desc]
The original “Return to the Sky” plan was disrupted, and the action that was supposed to raise the banner of resistance against the Empire was delayed again and again after losing Spitfire’s leadership. This made Sky Stinger, who had become the acting governer, extremely dissatisfied. His long-cherished “Friendship Journal” post-reading practice was interrupted by what seemed to be a dirty assassination plot most likely orchestrated by the Empire and its related forces.
Because of this, Sky Stinger, who was already an active proponent of promoting Harmonism, did not show any good attitude towards the Empire after becoming the acting governer. Despite Vapor Trail’s repeated reminders to recognize Stratusburg’s position, Sky Stinger not only publicly rejected the Empress’s assistance in the assassination investigation but also stopped participating in the “friendship salon” with Canterlot officials that Spitfire had to attend previously, citing the investigation as an excuse.
Soon, a letter from Canterlot by Fancy Pants arrived: “The Empire’s loyal governer Spitfire has encountered misfortune, and the Empress is sleepless day and night, tossing and turning, worrying about the safety of Stratusburg’s residents. It is recommended that Stratusburg hold a governer by-election immediately to appease the public.” Fancy Pants wrote in the letter that the Empire has always supported the autonomy of the Stratusburg Dominion and would respect the choices of Stratusburg’s residents. Attached to the letter was a specific proposal, which included: Canterlot hoped that Stratusburg could complete the election within 4 months, suggested that the acting governer avoid conflicts of interest, and prevent the ruling party from using its position to campaign for the election or suppress voters. Finally, Fancy Pants listed some candidates recommended by the Empire: “The Washouts” Lightning Dust, Director of the Meteorological Bureau Feather Flatterfly, Miss Laurette Dove, followed by dozens of Canterlot officials.
Sky Stinger sat in Spitfire’s office, and after hearing Vapor Trail read the two letters from the Empire, he slammed his hoof on the table in anger, almost smashing the dent that had just been repaired.

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_43_o0]
Is this how the Empire call “autonomy”?

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_43_TOOLTIP]
Unlock a §Rtimed§! series of decisions: §RAfter the Gunshot§!.

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_44]
Testimony of Short Fuse

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_44_desc]
Sky Stinger and Vapor Trail soon rushed to the police station. Through the thin cloud layer covering the one-way glass window, they saw Short Fuse sitting in the interrogation room. He was no longer the flamboyant and irritable pony he used to be. Whether it was due to guilt for his mistakes or the “success” of Harmonism education, Short Fuse had become taciturn and even a bit timid.
Before Sky Stinger could speak, Short Fuse had already opened up: “It was... it was me... I didn’t mean to... I don’t know what happened —” As he began to deflect responsibility, Sky Stinger slammed the table: “You don’t know? Were you sent here on a mission by Lightning Dust?” At this moment, Sky Stinger only needed a name. As long as he could prove that Short Fuse still had ties to Lightning Dust, he could take the initiative to eradicate the Washouts anti-Harmonism force. Or, if Short Fuse was acting on the Empire’s orders... then the “Return to the Sky” plan could be put back on the agenda.
Vapor Trail, seeing this, took out the glass shards from the bottle at the crime scene and gave them to Sky Stinger. He then displayed them to Short Fuse and sternly questioned, “Tell me, what is this?!”
Short Fuse looked at the glass shards, then at Sky Stinger glaring at him, and finally at Vapor Trail, whose eyes were filled with disappointment. He was momentarily speechless. Vapor Trail and Sky Stinger had now become the classic good cop-bad cop duo. Vapor Trail stepped forward and gently patted Short Fuse’s back, “Relax. Before it shattered, was the bottle filled with ‘Pegasus Joy Juice’? If it was, don’t be afraid. We will help you through drug treatment for this problem.”
Short Fuse looked at Vapor Trail but didn’t dare to speak. Sky Stinger, however, didn’t want this incident to turn from an assassination orchestrated by hostile forces into a tragedy of a single pony addicted to “Pegasus Joy Juice”, so he continued to press: “If you can tell us where the ‘Pegasus Joy Juice’ in this bottle came from, we will let you go. Did the Empire give it to you? Or did Lightning Dust give it to you? Choose one!”
“I... I got it from the Empire!”, Short Fuse hesitated and finally said it. Sky Stinger immediately noted it down. Vapor Trail, however, looked at Short Fuse in confusion, seemingly unable to understand why he would have any connection with the Empire. “Are you telling the truth?” Vapor Trail continued to pat Short Fuse’s back, asking in a gentle tone.

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_44_o0]
“...”

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_45]
Timbucktu Merchant

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_45_desc]
Soon after the crystal industry was completely opened up, the registered merchants under Wind Rider and his Chamber of Commerce quickly monopolized the mining, processing, and sales of crystals in Timbucktu. The Cloudsdale Chamber of Commerce has almost transformed into the Timbucktu Chamber of Commerce.
But the merchants’ desires never stop at monopolizing one industry, and the members of the Chamber of Commerce began to look at various industries in Cloudsdale and its surrounding areas: the catering business in Cloudsdale, the arms business of the Washouts, the “Pegasus Joy Juice” from the Rainbow Factory, and the heating industry of the Weather Factory... They want it all.
This is the true impact and final result of the monopoly rights that Wind Rider demanded, a behemoth powerful enough to intervene in the Timbucktu region and even the entire Stratusburg with just financial strength. Besides financial influence, Wind Rider is also actively seeking political influence, overly enthusiastically trying to cooperate with the Stratusburg government and participate in every action of the government...

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_45_o0]
See how rampant they can get

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_46]
Timbucktu Merchant

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_46_desc]
Soon after the crystal industry was completely opened up, the registered merchants under Wind Rider and his Chamber of Commerce quickly monopolized the mining, processing, and sales of crystals in Timbucktu. The Cloudsdale Chamber of Commerce has almost transformed into the Timbucktu Chamber of Commerce.
But the merchants’ desires never stop at monopolizing one industry, and the members of the Chamber of Commerce began to look at various industries in Cloudsdale and its surrounding areas: the catering business in Cloudsdale, the arms business of the Washouts, the “Pegasus Joy Juice” from the Rainbow Factory, and the heating industry of the Weather Factory... They want it all.
This is the result that Feather Flatterfly’s “free trade” failed to foresee — unrestricted competition always leads to a winner that takes all. Now, Wind Rider not only almost exclusively enjoys all the benefits of Feather Flatterfly’s reforms, but is also preparing to merge the Weather Factory into the Chamber of Commerce. It’s no wonder that Feather Flatterfly’s reforms failed to be implemented in the Empire — given the Empire’s tangled web of interests, Feather Flatterfly’s “free trade” was just a new way for those secret police and noble bureaucrats to make money. Although Warm Light Flow’s rejection of Feather Flatterfly’s proposal may have been out of self-interest, it inadvertently avoided a tragedy.

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_46_o0]
See how rampant they can get

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_47]
A Little Note from Vapor Trail

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_47_desc]
“Governor Spitfire, I’m sorry I deceived you...”
“About the ‘Return to the Sky’ plan we discussed in the meeting, I don’t have much confidence in it. After analyzing the attitude of the Cantelot officials and assessing the Empire’s current idle military strength, we believe that the Empire will not sit idly by, but will instead increase its intervention in Stratusburg. After evaluating the military strength, even our most proud air force will have no chance of competing with the Empire.”
“I kept this from you because I didn’t want to disappoint Sky Stinger too much. He has read the Friendship Diary too many times and thinks about these things every day. I once wanted him to analyze it calmly, but we ended up parting ways unhappily.”
“Therefore, I implore you: for the sake of Stratusburg, please do not carry out the ‘Return to the Sky’ plan. For the sake of Sky Stinger, please do not expose my lie. I can provide you with an excuse to refuse to implement the plan, and this excuse is by no means another lie, but a real hidden danger:”
“Be cautious of Wind Rider! We previously mentioned that the plan itself has received enthusiastic support from Wind Rider, but after background investigation, I found that the arms business that Wind Rider’s Chamber of Commerce is engaged in is not as independent or competitive with the Washouts as we originally envisioned — the Washouts IS one of Wind Rider’s main suppliers.”
“This means that the part in our ‘Return to the Sky’ plan about eliminating the Washouts may have already been leaked to them by Wind Rider, and they may have further leaked the entire plan to the Empire...”
“Of course, I understand that it is difficult to suddenly stop the mission once it has started. But I still hope to continue discussing this matter with you.”

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_47_o0]
Okay

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_48]
Into the Hurricane

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_48_desc]
“First of all, we must send our blessings to the still unconscious Spitfire.” Lightning Dust cleared her throat and spoke to the audience. Beside the Unicorn Mountain, near Cloudsdale, the “Washouts” were organizing a new performance — the first since Lightning Dust announced her candidacy for the Stratusburg by-election. Although their performances used to be enjoyed only by a few rebellious foals or some minority pegasi, this time it was filled with well-dressed pegasi politicians, clearly indicating that this was more than just a performance. Also because of this, even though everypony knew that Lightning Dust and Spitfire had a bad relationship, she still had to say a few good words for Spitfire at this moment.
“What happened to Spitfire is unfortunate, but we must move on. The by-election in Stratusburg is both a test and an opportunity. It is an opportunity for us pegasi...”
Then, Lightning Dust talked about the ancient Pegasi city of Timbucktu, which was once the pride of the pegasi but was destroyed by Queen Chrysalis’s attack. Lightning Dust blamed it on complacency: the wealth brought by the crystal business made the pegasi, who once soared in the clouds, forget their mission and live in the city with their wings folded, losing their courage to fly through generations of comfort. And Lightning Dust — who claimed to be a descendant of Timbucktu — did not want to see pegasi repeating the tragic history now after a thousand years. Then, she announced the most important item of her campaign program: the Hurricane plan.
Lightning Dust planned to integrate all of Stratusburg and Cloudsdale, establishing a huge “flight training camp” exclusively for pegasi, which she called the New Timbucktu. A place where, the only things that would determine pegasi’s lives would be the speed and height of their flight, not the amount of wealth or the rank of their positions; a place where, pegasi would gain everything through flying, not by struggling on the ground under the shadow of the Windigos; a place where, pegasi would guard their homeland with the “Hurricane” they created themselves. Specifially, Lightning Dust presented several research proposals from the Weather Laboratory: research on generating electricity through hurricanes, research on dispersing Windigos with hurricanes, militarization of hurricanes, and the combination of hurricanes and pegasi flying abilities...
“... We choose to fly into the hurricane. We choose to fly into the hurricane in a few yaers and do the other things, not because they are easy, but because they are hard; because that goal will serve to organize and measure the best of our energies and skills, because that challenge is one that we are willing to accept, one we are unwilling to postpone, and one which we intend to win, and the others, too.”

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_48_o0]
Okay

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_48_TOOLTIP]
Unlock §Rtimed§! decison in §YAfter the Gunfire§!: §YProhibit the Washouts Tour§!

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_49]
Vapor Trail’s Analysis · I

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_49_desc]
As Sky Stinger was about to restart the declaration of war against the Empire based on the testimony of Short Fuse, Vapor Trail stopped him: “Sky Stinger, double-check this.”
Seeing Sky Stinger’s puzzled expression, Vapor Trail sighed: “How many times have I told you to read less of the ‘Friendship Diary’ and read more of the books by Cozy Glow and Canterlot? Their ideas may not be correct, but their political wisdom is obviously more helpful for our survival than that fairy tale-like story by Princess Twi —”
Sky Stinger’s expression immediately darkened, and he looked at Vapor Trail with annoyance. “What’s your point?”
Vapor Trail, realizing the situation, immediately stopped her subjective nonsense about Princess Twilight’s masterpiece and picked up Short Fuse’s testimony again: “If Short Fuse was really sent by the Empire, why didn’t he escape back to the Empire that night but instead came to confess the next day? How could the Empire allow that?”
Sky Stinger opened his mouth to object but found no rebuttal, falling into thought instead. Seizing the moment, Vapor Trail continued deliberately: "I believe Short Fuse was more likely sent by the ‘Washouts’, to assassinate Spitfire and then blame it on the Empire. Their goal was to set us against the Empire. Wind Rider is not our ally; he may have leaked the plan to the ‘Washouts’, giving them an opportunity.”
Sky Stinger’s confusion only deepened: “The Washouts? Isn’t the Washouts in cahoots with the Empire? Besides, we were going to go to war with the Empire anyway. Why go through all this trouble?”
Vapor Trail shook her head and sighed.

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_49_o0]
“You still don’t get it.”

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_50]
Vapor Trail’s Analysis · II

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_50_desc]
“Rolling Thunder worked for the Empire once, but Lightning Dust never did. Lightning Dust is just a lunatic, neither on our side nor on the Empire’s. Eliminating the ‘Washouts’ was once part of our ‘Return to the Sky’ plan, but now, with the by-election in Stratusburg, if Lightning Dust can become join the plan instead of becoming the target, she will not only avoid conflict but also be able to hedge her bets on both sides.” Vapor Trail explained to Sky Stinger, who was still in the dark, without any impatience.
“So... you’re suggesting that we eliminate the ‘Washouts’ before declaring war on the Empire?” Sky Stinger asked.
“Not quite. Lightning Dust has already announced her participation in the by-election of Stratusburg. If we take military action against her, it would look like we are persecuting a political competitor. Although the citizens of Stratusburg support us, this would give the Empire a reason to intervene.”
“Isn’t that just perfect to go against the Empire —” Sky Stinger was about to interrupt Vapor Trail, but she interrupted him again. Vapor Trail rolled her eyes at him, almost imperceptibly, and continued:
“We have to first publicize Short Fuse’s crimes and the connection between him and the ‘Washouts’ through unofficial channels, create an atmosphere, and win the by-election — we will easily win, there’s no doubt about it — then we can deal with Lightning Dust, and finally expose the Empire through Rolling Thunder. We have to take it step by step, like flying cloud by cloud, Sky Stinger.”

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_50_o0]
Sky Stinger ought to have understood... right?

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_51]
The Sepal Files: Wind Rider

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_51_desc]
The information obtained by Vapor Trail from the Sepal indicates that Wind Rider is betting on both sides: on the one hoof, he publicly supports Sky Stinger and the current government of Stratusburg; on the other hoof, he has also introduced many members of the Chamber to attend Lightning Dust’s performances and banquets...
For a businesspony, this behavior is quite normal, as they only care about maximizing profits and minimizing risks. But does Wind Rider’s behavior represent the attitude of more groups? Is it possible that our inflated approval rating is just a bunch of fence-sitters filling in the gaps?
It is worth closely monitoring Wind Rider’s subsequent actions and the mainstream attitude of the Cloudsdale Chamber of Commerce. At the same time, we must also pay attention to counter-surveillance. If Wind Rider realizes that the Stratusburg authorities are monitoring competitors and their supporters, this kind of public opinion influence may be something we cannot afford.

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_51_o0]
Okay

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_52]
The Sepal Files: Suspect of the Assassination Case

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_52_desc]
After a month, Vapor Trail finally compiled the investigation results of the Sepal organization into a report and handed it to Sky Stinger. However, it was difficult to draw any conclusions from the report: no pony could escape suspicion.
Lightning Dust stood as the prime suspect. As leader of the Washouts and Short Fuse’s direct superior, she had not only motive but opportunity. Her suspiciously well-prepared campaign materials immediately following Spitfire’s assassination only deepened the cloud of suspicion around her.
Wind Rider ranked next - everypony knew the unscrupulous merchant’s insatiable greed. Though he'd already secured considerable influence, Spitfire’s proposed regulations against commercial monopolies had threatened his empire. The businesspony always hungered for more.
Then there’s the Sire’s Hollow — taking over the Rainbow Factory was part of the “Return to the Sky” plan. They may have heard it from the Chamber of Commerce and wanted to take action first — after all, Short Fuse’s outburst may have come from the influence of “Pegasus Joy Juice”, which is a product of the Sire’s Hollow Rainbow Factory.
Then came Feather Flatterfly, the Empire’s envoy to Stratusburg. His Weather Factory acquisition plans had clashed directly with Spitfire’s decisions. The diplomat might well have hired an assassin. Worse, he could be backed by Fancy Pants.
Even the gentle and kind Miss Laurette Dove cannot be cleared — the Dove family have been struggling about their enterprise recently. She had some unsuccessfully attempted expansions into crystal industry and Rainbow Factory, beaten to the punch by her competitors. Before the secret meeting, Sky Stinger and Vapor Trail saw her having an unpleasant conversation with Spitfire. It was also during that encounter that she knocked over Sky Stinger and saw the secret documents about the “Return to the Sky” plan. In fact, according to the records of the Stratusburg City Hall, the last pony Spitfire met before being shot was exactly Miss Laurette.
In summary, this report did not provide any conclusions, but instead made all factions in Stratusburg suspicious. Even more so, Lightning Dust is spreading rumors that Spitfire’s assassination is a power grab conspiracy by Sky Stinger and Vapor Trail, trying to drag them down too.

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_52_o0]
So confusing

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_53]
Honored Guest

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_53_desc]
When the crystal industry’s profits had been nearly divided up, Wind Rider set his sights on the next opportunity — the newly established Weather Bureau and its subsidiaries: the Weather Factory and the New Weather Laboratory.
Upon entering Spitfire’s office, Wind Rider found her already waiting with steaming Starswirl coffee prepared. As he took his first sip, barely having a chance to swallow, Spitfire cut straight to the chase: “The Weather Factory, just drop it. I’m handing it over to Feather Flatterfly.”
Wind Rider nearly spat out his coffee, sitting bolt upright, coughing violently as the hot liquid went down wrong. Seizing the moment while he recovered, Spitfire pressed on without letting him respond: “I don’t trust Imperial officials. But the Empire won’t be throwing its weight around Stratusburg much longer. By assigning the factory to Feather Flatterfly now, we’ll have grounds to reclaim it for ourselves later. I’ve already discussed this with him this morning. This matter doesn’t concern you, and we don’t want you be the one sitting at the table when we reclaim the Weather Factory. It’s just business. I hope you understand.”
Wind Rider sat stunned for several seconds. Just as he opened his mouth to protest — “But that’s not why I called you here,” Spitfire interjected smoothly. “The Rainbow Factory... I need you to have a word with Miss Laurette about...”

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_53_o0]
Each to own jobs

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_54]
Honored Guest

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_54_desc]
Feather Flatterfly had been in Stratusburg for some time, but this marked his first meeting with Spitfire, the Governor of the Stratusburg Dominion.
The impeccably groomed diplomat settled across from Spitfire’s desk, eyed the steaming Starswirl coffee, and discreetly pushed it aside. After a measured glance at his host, he launched into his presentation: “Since the implementation of free trade in Stratusburg, economic growth...”
Spitfire watched as Feather produced spreadsheet after spreadsheet — line graphs, pie charts, statistical models — barely suppressing a yawn. Her wings twitched impatiently against the desk. What a tedious bureaucrat, she thought.
“... if the Weather Bureau initiates market-oriented reforms for the Weather Factory, we project that within months we could —”
“Wind Rider.” Spitfire finally cut through the droning presentation. “I’m giving the Weather Factory to Wind Rider. In fact, I’ll be meeting him this afternoon.” She leaned forward, her voice dropping. “Because we both know your privatization would just end with the Chamber of Commerce buying everything anyway.”
Feather blinked, momentarily taken aback. “True, the Chamber of Commerce’s monopolistic practices warrant our attention. But I believe that with the market’s self-regulation and the introduction of external competitors, we can break —”
Spitfire interrupted again, her tone firm: “That’s not the point. I didn’t invite you here for that. It’s about the Rainbow Factory. I need you to have a word with Miss Laurette about...”

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_54_o0]
Each to own jobs

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_55]
A Little Note from Vapor Trail

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_55_desc]
“Governor Spitfire, I have conducted an investigation into the Weather Factory as you requested.”
“Long story short, I believe the Weather Factory is not suitable for either Feather Flatterfly or Wind Rider. The unions here are very independent and united, just like Stratusburg. The Weather Factory is a rebellious area; neither the big capitalists nor the Empire’s bureaucrats have ever tamed this place, and I don’t think Feather or Wind Rider would be an exception. However, I suggest you let them compete against each other: tell Feather that you’ll give the Weather Factory to Wind Rider, and tell Wind Rider that you’ll give it to Feather. Then we can see what they offer.”
“Ultimately, the Weather Factory will still be managed by the unions, and we need to start negotiating with them in advance. One possible path is that if Wind Rider wins, we can publicly cooperate with the unions to take him down in the name of anti-monopoly. If Feather wins, we can secretly win over the unions under the pretext of opposing the Empire and sideline him.”
“Of course, these are just my humble opinions. I know you will make a better choice.”

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_55_o0]
Okay

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_56]
New Unicorn · II

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_56_desc]
...buzz buzz... (TV noise)
“—— We are witnessing the birth of another unicorn! Of course, this is not to say that another little pony with a horn and magic has been born, but rather a rising unicorn company!” The field reporter said enthusiastically.
Starswirl Coffee, a small family coffee shop that has only recently emerged, has gained the favor of several discerning members of the Chamber of Commerce with its high-priced, high-quality coffee aimed at the high-end market. To explore the reasons for Starswirl Coffee’s explosive popularity, we interviewed the owner of the small coffee shop.
“Our secret? Oh, just unicorn tears and moon-roasted beans. But mostly, it’s about EXCLUSIVITY! When Miss Laurette said our latte ‘tasted like memory of harmony’, we knew we’d made it. And somehow, the Stratusburg government heard about it. Now they use our coffee on entertaining all their VIPs, Miss Laurette, Feather Flatterfly, and Wind Rider, who is now not only our customer but also our largest shareholder. It’s not just coffee — it’s a LIFESTYLE.” The owner of Starswirl Coffee said with a wink, and she’s right! This unwritten standard for entertaining VIPs in the Stratusburg government immediately became popular in Stratusburg and even the Greater Cloudsdale area.
However, not all customers are coffee lovers, they just want to be part of the trend. “In the future, all ponies will drink their fruit!” said by Stellar Flare, the second largest shareholder of Starswirl Coffee, proposing to the owner of Starswirl Coffee to add Sire’s Hollow fruit juice to the menu.
“Anyway,” The field reporter concluded, “as Starswirl plans its IPO, investors eagerly await shares in what analysts call ‘the first caffeine-based Ponzi scheme’. Meanwhile, the rest of us will be here, spending our weekly salary on a cup of coffee just to take a picture and upload them to the cloud. Back to the studio.”

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_56_o0]
Okay

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_57]
New Unicorn · I

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_57_desc]
...buzz buzz... (TV noise)
“—— We are witnessing the birth of another unicorn! Of course, this is not to say that another little pony with a horn and magic has been born, but rather a rising unicorn company!” The field reporter said enthusiastically.
The Timbucktu Crystal Rushers, a subsidiary of the Cloudsdale Chamber of Commerce, suddenly became the focus of various investors within a year due to the explosive popularity of Timbucktu crystal jewelry: If it was safe to say that most noble ponies of Canterlot had never heard of the name Timbucktu before, now anypony who couldn’t find this small town on the map at first glance could basically say goodbye to their career as a business consultant.
“The Crystal Rushers were originally the Weather Factory Labor Union, funded by Miss Laurette.” Wind Rider said in an interview, “Miss Laurette is a very kind and visionary pony, and she was the one who provided me with my starting capital. It’s just a pity that her business acumen still needs to be improved. Due to the union’s long-term free legal assistance, it was running at a loss, and eventually I negotiated with Miss Laurette and agreed to buy the union and take on all its debts.”
“I was the first to realize the potential of the Timbucktu crystal business, you know, I’m always the fastest. It was true when I was in the Wonderbolts, and it’s true now in business.” Wind Rider said, feeling very satisfied with himself. “So I had the union’s members move from the Weather Factory to Timbucktu to mine for gold, uh... crystals, to be more accurate. This way they can use the crystals as payment to the union for legal assistance.”
However, not all ponies are in favor of the Crystal Rushers’ approach.
“The sole purpose of a labor union is to organize workers to negotiate with monopolistic companies, but now it has become part of a monopolistic company. I’m worried this will cause dissatisfaction among the workers, especially those Weather Factory workers who refuse to move.” Miss Laurette, perhaps slightly displeased for missing out on this opportunity, commented.
“The Crystal Rushers are monopolizing the mining industry in Timbucktu, which is unhealthy.” The Empire’s Chief Economic Advisor, Feather Flatterfly, commented, “For example, just like Canterlot. The cosmetics industry in Canterlot is monopolized by the Fleur de Lis company. In the early stages, this brought a lot of employment and tax revenue, but soon the monopoly caused the Empire’s economy to falter—”
“Beep—” Without warning, the live broadcast was cut off by Canterlot.

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_57_o0]
Okay

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_58]
iHorn: Magical, But Not That Magical.

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_58_desc]
§g(A minimalist rap beat with heavy bass)§!
You’re an Earth Pony. You graze. You grow apples.
You’re a Pegasus. You fly. You move clouds.
You’re fine. You’re good. But deep down, there’s always been that one thing missing.

Introducing iHorn.
§g(Rap: Magic. Magic. Magic. Magic.)§!
§g(Showing off a smooth reflective aluminum alloy casing)§!
A slight glow. §g(Ponies from different ethnic backgrounds dancing around a bonfire)§!
A subtle push. §g(A Pegasus flying high in the sky, pushing clouds away with magic)§!
A gentle touch. §g(An Earth pony using magic to levitate a book)§!
Move that carrot. Open that door. Light that candle.
“I didn’t have magic. Now I connect to iMagic, and enjoy iFriendship.”

§g(Rap: Magic. Magic. Magic. Magic.)§!
Privacy. It’s built in.
Tested by Changelings, the masters of incognito.
Comfort. It’s lightweight.
Approved by Dr. Hooves, the leading expert in pony head ergonomics.
Charging. It’s wireless.
Like Tirek, it sucks the energy right out of the air.
And most importantly.

It comes in Twilight Purple and Cozy Pink, of course.
§g(Showing off iHorn Pro and iHorn Max)§!

§g(Rap: Magic. Magic. Magic. Magic. This is the biggest horn of the summer.)§!
iHorn. Magical, but not that magical.

§g(This product, a result of collaborative investment and development among Ponyville, Cloudsdale, and Las Pegasus, was conceived under the technical leadership of Dr. Hooves. The product testing phase has successfully incorporated high-altitude adaptability verification in Stratusburg and undergone rigorous meteorological compatibility testing in Cloudsdale. The theoretical framework and foundational design inspiration for the product integrate Ponyville's traditional magical technology with contemporary innovations derived from Storm King Island. The realized magical capabilities of the iHorn are subject to variation based on the purchaser's equine classification (race), inherent individual physiological differences, and adherence to applicable local statutory regulations. It is explicitly noted that full support for all advertised magical functionalities may not be available across all geographic regions. Users are strongly advised to consult prevailing local magical usage regulations prior to deployment. This device is explicitly engineered to foster cultural exchange and mutual understanding among diverse equine populations, strictly maintaining a principle of neutrality and abstaining from involvement in any regional political matters, including, but not limited to, jurisdictional conflicts between the Empire and the Resistance, and inter-species disagreements involving Changelings and Zebras. We maintain an institutional commitment against all forms of belligerence and conflict. The diverse, multi-racial harmonious scenarios depicted in promotional materials are solely intended to illustrate the product's inclusive design philosophy. All operational magical energy is supplied via the integrated magical core and supplemental external charging mechanisms. Activation of the wireless charging function requires placement within specifically designated magical energy transmission fields. The iHorn incorporates precision magical components and is thus unsuitable for sustained operation in environments characterized by excessive moisture, particulate contamination (e.g., mud), or extreme meteorological events. Direct exposure to intense magical interference sources, such as dark rocks, must be strictly avoided. All visual media production adhered to the exclusive use of sustainably sourced, renewable materials, ensuring that no sentient or non-sentient living organisms were subjected to harm. The final authority for interpretation of this document and product specifications rests solely with Dr. Hooves Laboratory. © Dr. Hooves Laboratory. All rights reserved. For all inquiries pertaining to legal or intellectual property matters, please direct correspondence to the Las Pegasus Consortium’s Legal Department. The claim that foals were employed in the production of iHorn is a false rumor, and the Las Pegasus Consortium reserves the right to pursue legal action.)§!

[en.EVENT_C04_MAIN_58_o0]
?

[en.PIHC_IHORN]
iHorn

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_1]
发展与否，这是个问题

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_1_desc]
《层云堡小餐馆扩建计划》《帝国征兵办通知》《廷马克图水晶开采方案》《云中城关于层云堡马芬出口质量问题的投诉》... 喷火在办公室内，看着一摞摞的报告，烦躁地甩着她的口哨。
随着呆蹄领导下的云中城逐渐进入福利社会，没有生存压力，也没有增长空间，更多具有野心、有能力的小马开始在层云堡寻找机会。但是，涌入的投机者对于层云堡来说却不见得是好事：喷火清楚，层云堡能存活至今的最重要原因不是军事强大，而是经济落后：帝国从征服层云堡获取的预计收益甚至不够弥补镇压的开支。一旦层云堡经济发展，帝国入侵的利益增加，层云堡的生存反而会更加困难。
此前，喷火对这些发展提案的态度大多是“不予理睬”，但是，越来越多的小马开始询问，为什么不批准这些百利而无一害的提案呢？天真的层云堡居民们从不质疑喷火的领导，但仅仅是出于好奇的询问，也让喷火不知该怎么回答。仅仅因为害怕帝国的入侵，从此就不再发展，这是一个正确的选择吗？
喷火甩着口哨，开始一个个地翻阅这些报告。

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_1_o0]
是时候做出些改变了。

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_2]
《层云堡小餐馆扩建计划》

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_2_desc]
由破空与雾轨经营的层云堡小餐馆，长久以来是层云堡居民夜生活的重要组成部分，即使是喷火自己也会隔三差五地来这里与居民们共同干杯庆祝。不过，破空提交的这份报告显示，因为小餐馆对层云堡居民的价格实惠，所以小餐馆的盈利本身并不算太高。破空希望扩建小餐馆，面向不仅仅是层云堡，而且是整个大云中城地区开放，以提升小餐馆的盈利能力。在报告中，破空相信这不仅仅是为了金币，也是为了扩大层云堡本土品牌的知名度。
除此之外，破空还在报告中提出了一个更加大胆的设想：云中城在呆蹄领主的统治下，对马芬的需求越来越高，层云堡一直保持着对云中城的小规模马芬出口。破空希望通过扩建小餐馆，进而开设专门的马芬工坊，他评估呆蹄会像一个无底洞一样接受层云堡输出的所有马芬，这将是一个巨大的商机。更进一步，提案表示扩建餐馆的费用由破空与雾轨自行承担，喷火不需要为此担心。
破空与雾轨是喷火的老朋友了，早在闪电天马学院时期，喷火是教练，而破空与雾轨则是最优秀的学生之二。训练时，破空时常做出一些鲁莽的决定，但他的飞行能力总是足以让他逃脱后果；雾轨则是一个非常稳重的飞行员，在训练中通常保持低调与谨慎。但这次的提案仅仅来自于破空，并没有雾轨的签名，这值得注意。

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_2_o0]
帮助我们的老朋友...？

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_3]
《帝国征兵办通知》

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_3_desc]
喷火并没怎么仔细看，直接翻到了下一份报告...

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_3_o0]
下次一定

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_4]
《廷马克图水晶开采方案》

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_4_desc]
这是来自云中城商业委员会的提案，他们在廷马克图遗址发现了一些浅层水晶矿，储量巨大且质量很高、花纹精美适合制成首饰，利润巨大...
然而，来自云中城的贪婪资本家们对层云堡并不了解，在此生活数年的喷火则略有了解：廷马克图是在两姐妹政权的初期层云堡地区的一个天马城邦，并与那时的小马利亚王国关系密切，以盛产香料（辣味的彩虹）闻名。廷马克图的国王无意间发现了那些“被诅咒的水晶”，廷马克图的水晶首饰生意爆火，也招来了幻形灵王国的觊觎 —— 幻形灵并不食用香料，但水晶则意味着财富。曾经毫无价值的小城邦廷马克图一夜之间变得富有，也在顷刻之间在幻形灵的攻势下消失的无影无踪。
因此，有着这样不详预兆的廷马克图水晶，制成首饰是不会有消费者的，更不用说是利润巨大了。商业委员会自然不知道这些，即使用这种历史传说来反对他们，也只会被他们视作无稽之谈，或者干脆让我们隐瞒这些故事。自他们被呆蹄领主赶出云中城后，商业委员会的行事更加失去了规则约束，他们对于层云堡的提案也越来越唯利是图... 喷火看着这份提案，叹了口气，把它放到了一边。

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_4_o0]
暂不批准

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_5]
《云中城关于层云堡马芬出口质量问题的投诉》

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_5_desc]
层云堡与云中城的呆蹄领主一直保持着小规模的马芬贸易，但是，最近云中城的居民们开始抱怨，层云堡的杯糕质量下降，甚至出现了食品安全事件 —— 有的云中城小马在冷藏杯糕时竟然发生了杯糕爆炸！
喷火看着这份报告，皱起了眉头。马芬？爆炸？喷火又想起了破空的《层云堡小餐馆扩建计划》。也许... 正规化马芬生产流程，打造属于层云堡的高质量品牌，现在看似乎还是一个比较重要的发展方向。

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_5_o0]
我们会调查

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_6]
淘汰者巡回演出

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_6_desc]
新元年刚过没多久的一个下午，喷火的办公室大门突然被撞开，三只穿着飞行服带着头盔的天马冲了进来，后面跟着的是惊慌失措的保安。
“你们最好有重要的事情要说。” 喷火厌恶地挥了挥蹄子，示意保安退下。
领头的天马摘下头盔，是“淘汰者”飞行杂技表演队的队长闪尘，跟在两侧的则是滚雷与火药桶，他们是“淘汰者”的核心成员。“淘汰者”飞行杂技表演队大多是被闪电天马队开除的前学员或前队员，而且被开除的原因不能是能力不足，而是危险飞行或者不合群。他们自诩是“最具有天赋的天马”，不愿被闪电天马队迂腐的规则束缚，于是自行组建了“淘汰者”飞行杂技表演队。

“新元年快乐？喷火领长？” 闪尘带着颇有嘲笑的口吻飞到桌前，滚雷与火药桶则来到桌子两边将喷火围在中间。喷火没做任何回应，甚至没有摘下她的墨镜。
“醒醒，老东西！我们有帝国秩序部的批准，要在层云堡办一场庆祝新元年的巡回演出！” 闪尘重重地拍了一下桌子，将喷火桌面上的报告震得散落一地。“或许都算不上巡回，层云堡这种小地方，一场演出就够了。” 滚雷跟着嘲讽道。

喷火扫了扫桌子上的文件，看到桌子上已经被闪尘砸出了一个凹痕，她便直接没好气地回应：“你们巡回演出的门票钱得拿来赔偿这张桌子。至于多余的部分 — 你们自己掏钱赔吧。”
见到喷火暗示自己的演出挣不到门票钱，闪尘轻蔑地笑了一声，向滚雷使了个眼色转身离开。滚雷拍下巡回演出海报和两枚水晶钻石放在桌上，似有嫉妒般打量着喷火，就带着火药桶离开了办公室。

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_6_o0]
这也太嚣张了！

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_7]
淘汰者档案：闪尘

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_7_desc]
闪尘，与云宝黛茜同届的闪电天马队学院学员，因为一次不顾安危的飞行制造了龙卷风误伤了路过的小马而被喷火开除。从那以后，她便组建了“淘汰者”。起初她只是进行一些危险的特技表演，但在表演中经常接触危险道具让她与一些售卖火药、大炮、飞镖、炸弹与喷火器的军火商结识。难以界定具体从什么时候开始，“淘汰者”就开始得到来自军火商的资金支持，我们只知道他们在演出中使用越来越危险的道具，并将它们宣传成非常炫酷的道具鼓励观众购买和模仿。虽然至今为止，还没有发生过严重的伤害事件，但是无论是曾经的帝国皇家委员会和云中城商业委员会、还是如今的呆蹄和层云堡当局，都并不完全认可“淘汰者”的行为。
如今，闪尘背后的金主可能是帝国与商业委员会的残余势力 —— 当他们从执政地位沦落到如今的反对党地位时，他们对于军火商和闪尘的危险行为态度就发生了急速转折。现在的商业委员会中可能有不少成员都是军火商的代理，而闪尘则是他们最靓丽的名片。相比于帝国和商业委员会，闪尘自己似乎也有着更大的野心... 她并非在意权力或金钱，而是对“天马的极致天赋”有着狂热的追求，为此不惜亲自进行越来越危险的飞行表演，也不惜与帝国、商业委员会甚至是部下滚雷、火药桶等阻拦她的任何反对者发生冲突。

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_7_o0]
不看了

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_7_o1]
下一页

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_8]
淘汰者档案：滚雷

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_8_desc]
相比于淘汰者的创建者闪尘，滚雷反而是淘汰者中最臭名昭著的一个。滚雷与闪尘一样不惧危险，她享受在危险边缘跳舞的刺激感觉，也是闪电天马学院历史上为数不多因为“在九百万伏高压电的雷暴中做滚筒翻转”而被开除的学员。当一只飞马有过这样的经历后，生活中的一切对她来说都不能再称得上刺激了。即使是加入淘汰者，她也并不可能满足于简单的表演，而是要在其他方面寻找刺激。
终末之战后，她主动选择接受皇家委员会的任命代理管理大云中城地区，成为了云中城临时安保队长。闪尘因不满足于听从权威而选择与滚雷分道扬镳，殊不知滚雷同样不满足于服从权威。滚雷直接私下联系了和煦光流女皇，成为女皇的眼线，在管理大云中城地区的同时，连皇家委员会也成为了她的监控目标。在政治场上的斗争，带给了滚雷意想不到的新刺激：荣华富贵纸醉金迷与对日益增长的权力的渴望，与时时刻刻被暗算出局的危机感，让这个不顾自身安危追求刺激的赌徒像是在雷暴中滚筒翻转一样拼命地向上攀爬。
直到——她宣布动用安保部队镇压天气工厂游行示威鲁莽的决定彻底引爆了云中城的政治危机，也让她的政治生涯走到了尽头。为平息云中城愈演愈烈的动荡，陷身于水晶战争泥潭的和煦光流决定暂时妥协，罢免了滚雷的职务以换取云中城的安宁。滚雷一夜之间从云中城大区区长变成了无名小卒，甚至遭到全城民众的唾弃，只得离开云中城回到闪尘的淘汰者队伍中，等待下一个机会的到来。
正如一个赌徒不可能因为输掉了一把牌而放弃赌局，短短两年的政治生涯让滚雷对权力的渴望已经深入骨髓。有证据表明明，闪尘与军火商的合作、更多灰色交易的背后，都有滚雷的身影。滚雷无疑才是淘汰者中，最受帝国青睐，也最危险的一位。

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_8_o0]
不看了

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_8_o1]
下一页

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_8_o2]
上一页

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_9]
淘汰者档案：火药桶

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_9_desc]
不同于前面两位野心巨大的领导者，火药桶算是淘汰者中相对平庸的一个。他在闪电天马学院中能力并不突出，被开除的原因是无法控制自己的脾气。
火药桶关心的只有自己，他的生活大概只有飞行、饮食与发脾气。对于利益，他斤斤计较；对于朋友，他也不会有太多的忠诚；对于飞行技术，只能说他从未考虑过减肥。
在淘汰者组建初期，火药桶因为看到闪尘的表演大受欢迎、门票销售利润巨大而加入了淘汰者；随后又因为权力和财富跟从滚雷，成为了云中城安保部队的一员。在滚雷升任云中城大区区长时，他便接替了滚雷的位置，成为了云中城安保部队的新领导者。在任期间，他没有做过什么如滚雷一样的坏事，但也没有做过什么好事，只管拿着帝国的薪水，搜刮着云中城的财富。当滚雷被解职时，小跟班火药桶也跟着失去了一切。
虽说如今商业委员会与淘汰者是关系亲密，但假若商业委员会要在淘汰者中培养内线，那火药桶绝对是他们最好的选择。商业委员会与层云堡当局都相信，只要给的足够多，身为淘汰者成员的火药桶也并不介意为其他组织合作。毕竟，这在历史上差点发生过。
唯一需要注意的，大概就是和他讨价还价的时候，要小心他的脾气。尽管难以置信，但是他真的有在努力控制自己的脾气了。

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_9_o0]
不看了

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_9_o1]
下一页

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_9_o2]
上一页

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_10]
淘汰者档案：云中城商业委员会

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_10_desc]
云中城商业委员会是一个历史非常复杂的团体，不同时期的商业委员会代表着完全不同的利益集团。早在皇家委员会刚刚接管大云中城地区的时候，云中城商业委员会就已经成立，那时委员会中的成员大多是来自坎特洛特的旧贵族，代表着奢侈品与时尚行业、高档餐饮业、以及新取得地位的女皇与帝国新军队的利益。随着滚雷等一批大云中城地区本地居民逐渐取得权力，商业委员会中也增添了更多云中城的新鲜面孔，开始偏好天气工厂等新兴轻工业。
羽蝶进入帝国担任首席经济顾问是商业委员会的一个重大转折 —— 滚雷失势后，羽蝶被准许在大云中城地区实践他的新经济理论，开启了长达一年的自由商业时代。在这一年中，云中城的经济迅速发展，但也因为缺乏监管而让闪尘代表的军火商、乘风代表的媒体财团等唯利是图的商马开始在云中城大肆横行。最终，呆蹄的当选终结了羽蝶前景广阔的实验，商业委员会从官方组织转变成了民间活动的商会。如今，云中城商业委员会几乎已经是乘风的私有商会，并尝试在层云堡、云中城等各个地区制造混乱，给自己旗下的企业创造趁虚而入的机会。

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_10_o0]
不看了

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_10_o1]
下一页

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_10_o2]
上一页

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_11]
淘汰者档案：水晶钻石

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_11_desc]
看完档案，喷火又打量起了桌上的两枚水晶钻石 —— 滚雷留下用于赔偿桌子的赔偿费。她拿起其中一枚，看着它在灯光下发散着犹如夜空中的星辰般的点点光芒。
等等，这好像就是廷马克图水晶！这很奇怪，“淘汰者”即使从事飞行特技表演和违法军火生意，也总是保持着流动，不太可能与采矿行业有什么瓜葛。这只能意味着，廷马克图水晶已经开始在市面上流通了。面对高额的利润，尽管没有获得喷火的批准，采矿业投机商们还是已经开始挖掘廷马克图水晶了...

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_11_o0]
不看了

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_11_o1]
上一页

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_12]
调查马芬出口

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_12_desc]
在云中城采购商交涉的过程中，他们向喷火展示了一批保留下来的马芬样品：这些马芬看起来很正常，但是遭遇剧烈的温度变化或者快速移动时就会发生爆炸。云中城方面表示这些马芬是从层云堡进口的，但喷火对层云堡的几家餐厅都了如指掌，这绝对不是层云堡的产品。
喷火原以为对方会要求层云堡提供完整的出口记录表、马芬厂商名单以证明这些马芬的来源，但来自但是... 价格呢？云中城代表接到的任务是带回尽可能多的马芬，因此他们直接表示了信任（大概是受到了伟大的呆蹄领主的指示），并进一步提出了将层云堡的马芬进口正式化、规模化的提案。喷火有些惊讶，但随即想起了来自破空与雾轨的层云堡餐厅扩张计划，这似乎是一个不错的机会。

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_12_o0]
成交...？

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_13]
《云中城-层云堡贸易协定》

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_13_desc]
云中城的代表再次来访，带回了呆蹄领主的旨意：她了解到层云堡居民许多是退役的闪电天马队成员或者闪电天马学院学员，于是提议云中城将闪电天马学院原址划归到层云堡管理，以此交换层云堡一年的马芬产量。如此，云中城不需要支付任何费用，而层云堡也可以获得闪电天马学院旧址。
自闪电天马队解散后，闪电天马学院也一直处于荒废状态... 直到呆蹄领主决定将这座空中小岛改造为马芬乐园。如今，闪电天马学院的多数飞行训练设施仍被保留，只是新增了一些马芬贴纸与玩偶，还额外开设了制作马芬的食堂...

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_13_o0]
听上去还不错

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_14]
《帝国征兵办通知》

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_14_desc]
由于上次的征兵通知没有得到回应，帝国再次向层云堡喷火办公室的垃圾桶发送了一份新的征兵通知。

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_14_o0]
下次一定

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_15]
《帝国征兵办通知》

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_15_desc]
由于上次的征兵通知没有得到回应，帝国再次向层云堡喷火办公室的垃圾桶发送了一份新的征兵通知。

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_15_o0]
下次一定

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_16]
《帝国征兵办通知》

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_16_desc]
由于上次的征兵通知没有得到回应，帝国再次向层云堡喷火办公室发送了一份新的征兵通知 —— 不过这一次，喷火想了想，还是拿起了这份征兵通知... 用来垫在桌子上防止中午的马芬午餐渣弄得满桌都是。

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_16_o0]
下次一定

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_17]
雾轨的提案

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_17_desc]
还没等喷火前去寻找雾轨，雾轨就已经飞进了喷火的办公室。
“如果我没猜错的话，你是为了破空的扩建计划而来的。破空最近怎么样？” 喷火摘下墨镜，看着面前的雾轨寒暄道。
“他... 他... 挺好的。” 雾轨似乎有些犹豫，随后立马将话题转到正事：“那个，关于破空的扩建计划... 其实，我隐瞒了他一些事情。”
喷火皱了皱眉头，示意雾轨继续说下去。
“我们在提案中提出扩建餐馆的费用自行承担... 但是我们并没有足够的资金。” 雾轨的声音越来越小，她似乎很担心喷火的反应。“我对餐馆扩大经营的收益很有信心，因此也不想仅仅因为没有启动资金而打击了破空的积极性... 所以，我想请您帮忙。我... 我... 可以申请一笔层云堡的贷款么？”

“那么大概需要多少？” 喷火看着雾轨，问道。
“初步估计... 如果要支持向云中城规模出口马芬，我们需要上游的供应链，还有冷藏仓库的建设，以及更大的厨房...” 雾轨思索着，完全陷入了自己的思考中。
喷火打断了她的思考：“报一个粗略的数字就可以了。”

“大概需要... 两万发展债券。”

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_17_o0]
我们考虑考虑

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_18]
《云中城-层云堡贸易协定》

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_18_desc]
经过我们与层云堡的沟通，对方同意以一年的免费马芬产量交换我们的闪电天马学院旧址。这样一来，我们不仅可以节省大量的费用，还能让闪电天马学院的旧址得到更好的利用。
自闪电天马队解散后，闪电天马学院也一直处于荒废状态... 直到不久前，这座空中小岛被改造为马芬乐园。如今，闪电天马学院的多数飞行训练设施仍被保留，只是新增了一些马芬贴纸与玩偶，还额外开设了制作马芬的食堂...

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_18_o0]
听上去还不错

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_18_o1]
先算了吧

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_19]
后台通行 · 上

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_19_desc]
在淘汰者巡回演出的当天，喷火也带着一队层云堡领导小马来到了演出现场，坐在了观众席的最前排。
表面上，喷火作为帝国任命的自治领领主，在以“欢庆新元年”为名义的巡回演出中必然要积极出席；实际上，喷火是来看笑话的。不出喷火的预料，层云堡的居民保持了团结：除了喷火带来的成员，没有一位层云堡居民出席了这次演出 —— 这意味着闪尘他们大概是赚不到门票钱了，更别说收回他们自费搭建的表演场地的成本了。

随着绿色的火焰被突然点燃，淘汰者的演出也开始了。闪尘带着滚雷与火药桶，出现在了舞台的中央。闪尘似乎也对此次演出的空座率并不意外，反而微笑着对前排的喷火一行鞠了一躬，便对着几乎空空如也的观众席开始了他们的特技表演。
在火圈、电锯、烟花与毒雾中，闪尘与滚雷辗转腾飞着，火药桶则在向他们投掷飞镖与爆炸马芬。对于他们来说，这是一个刺激的时刻，并不是因为表演 —— 而是因为藏在终点绿色火炬后的两把蹄铳。

闪尘一边飞行，一边不时用余光盯着喷火：她看到喷火仍坐在那里观看着表演，似乎还在享受着这场演出。“在你生命的最后时刻，好好欣赏被你开除的学员们的英姿吧。这些表演，都将是你余下不多的此生永远达不到的高度。” 闪尘心中窃喜道，与滚雷一起向终点的火炬飞去。

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_19_o0]
最后的直道冲刺

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_20]
后台通行 · 下

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_20_desc]
“砰——”
随着一声清脆而震耳欲聋的响声，会场的绿色火焰熄灭，闪尘与滚雷也在终点线处停下了他们的表演。
“发生什么事了？” 火药桶大喊着问道。他看向终点处的闪尘与滚雷，她们俩还没来得及拿出她们的蹄铳。

巨大的声响并非来自于蹄铳，而是来自于后台... 原来，早在演出开始前，喷火已经秘密安排一队层云堡警察突袭了“淘汰者”的后台。在后台，他们发现了各种危险道具、一些爆炸马芬、许多廷马克图水晶首饰和淘汰者与帝国的联系记录。

爆炸马芬与云中城反馈的样品一致，这意味着淘汰者就是造成云中城马芬爆炸事件的罪魁祸首。虽然因为没有造成伤亡，这不至于将他们关入大牢，但至少已经有了足够的理由将他们赶出层云堡。

廷马克图水晶首饰都是滚雷的个马收藏，这似乎是合法的购买，也并没有转售的迹象。滚雷将她的积蓄几乎都换成了这些首饰，似乎不是很符合一个寻求刺激不顾身外之物的淘汰者形象。但无论如何，这违反了喷火的廷马克图水晶禁售令，因此喷火选择了没收这些首饰。

而淘汰者与帝国的联系则表明... 已经有身份不明的小马利亚帝国的特工进入了层云堡。

当闪尘等淘汰者被层云堡警察带走时，闪尘与喷火的目光再次交叉，这一次，双方都没有说话，然而都在偷笑。似乎他们都认为对方并没有意识到自己的秘密。

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_20_o0]
精彩的表演

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_21]
对照组

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_21_desc]
“成功了！”
新天气实验室中的研究者们看着纸带上的数据激动地欢呼着 —— 纸带上的一个个用木炭黑烧出的黑点，此刻对他们来说却像太阳一般光明 —— 那是从天气工厂那边传输来的温度测量数据。庆祝声还尚未结束，更加热烈的喧闹声在实验室中爆发开来：借着实验的成功，研究小组内的一只小马向他暗恋已久的同事表白了。

“就像我们的实验一样，只要我们在一起，就能创造出奇迹”
小马说着，举起一束花。在他们的背后，纸带上的黑点依然在滚动，纸带转译员用木炭将+1.8抄写在实验室的玻璃板上 —— 他们的新生产线开工后，天气工厂地区的温度已经上升了1.8度。数年前，随着风之魔活动加剧和闪电天马队的解散，天气工厂的产能不再足以维持温暖；新生的坎特洛特政权此时也在与北方的冰雪之国交战。于是，和煦光流下令合并天气工厂与天气实验室，设立小马利亚帝国气象局，合作研究如何提高温度。只不过，气象局设立不久后，天气工厂的工马暴动就将这一项目几乎完全中断，天气实验室也在暴动中被破坏。直到喷火上台，重建天气实验室，双方的交流与研究才开始慢慢恢复。

“我想让我们的爱像新的生产线一样，永远热烈温暖；我想让我们的生活像纸带上的数据一样，越来越好！你... 愿意做我的女朋友吗？” 小马说着，将花递了上去；对面的同事也早已泪流满面。背后的玻璃板上，转译员又写下了数字+3.3。

“我愿意！”
此刻，连一直坚守职责的转译员看到这个画面也没有能忍住情绪，抓过纸带开始向天气工厂那边传输文字的编码信息：“天气实验室这边有小马表白了！~” 发完信息，转译员看着还在跳动的纸带，转身在玻璃板中写下了数字+5.6。很快，纸带停止了跳动，随后，天气工厂那边也开始传来文字的编码信息。应该是祝福语吧！转译员一把撤下新的纸带，开始转译上面黑点上的信息。

“天气工厂，祝二位 —— 额... 的长颈鹿鬃毛不会运输粉色的甜甜圈... 嗯？” 转译员看着纸带上的信息，一脸懵逼。随后他恍然大悟，纸带装反了！他赶忙将纸带正过来重新转译，这次，纸带上的信息是不堪入目的咒骂。

今夜的天气工厂，工马们在比原来低7度多的寒风中瑟瑟发抖。

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_21_o0]
冰箱轶事 —— 一对情侣科学家

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_22]
天使投资 · 上

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_22_desc]
喷火的办公室里，金边珐琅杯里的黑咖啡仍在冒热气。

喷火并不喜欢这种咖啡，更别提这杯价值三枚金币的星璇咖啡像贪婪的黑色漩涡般旋转着用掉了喷火的最后半罐方糖。当前层云堡资金紧张，气象学研究、小餐馆扩建、重建闪电天马学院，这每一项开销都是小小的层云堡当前无法支付的沉重负担，喷火更不可能花费额外的开销去享受奢侈的咖啡了。不，这杯咖啡是喷火为一位来客准备的，一位可以解决所有上述问题的来客。

不一会儿，一只一身黑色西装的雌性飞马，后面还带着两名保镖，走了进来。劳雷特·多芙，多芙家族的继承者。劳雷特小姐并不算富有，甚至比不上层云堡的一些商业委员会成员。但劳雷特小姐算是最他们之中最慷慨的一位 —— 也许仅次于曾经的瑞瑞。她从不介意将家族的资产投资到一些看不到什么短期回报的项目中去。事实上在塞拉斯蒂娅公主还当政的时代，劳雷特为闪电天马队提供了不少无偿资助；如今商业委员会中一些远远比劳雷特富裕的小马，都是从劳雷特哪里获得了第一桶金才发家致富的。此前几年，当层云堡从帝国拿到的补贴短一时间不足以支撑开销时，劳雷特也都会大方地为政府提供低息贷款，帮助层云堡渡过难关；在饥荒之时，劳雷特小姐也会自己出资购买粮食分发给民众。

因此，喷火非常有信心，劳雷特会帮助政府再次解决资金问题 —— 直到劳雷特小姐坐下，将面前的咖啡推到了一边。

劳雷特小姐凝视着墙上历届小马利亚运动会赞助商名单中排行首位镶着金边的“劳雷特·多芙”牌子，许久才开口，语气中仍带着迟疑。

“额...我不得不说你们提出的餐馆扩建计划非常具有吸引力，”

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_22_o0]
“但是...？”

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_23]
天使投资 · 下

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_23_desc]
“喷火领长，希望您能理解...” 随着劳雷特的解释，喷火才得知，因为劳雷特长期以来的慈善式投资，多芙家族在西部的业务几乎没什么增长，甚至还有所缩减。因此，如今的劳雷特也不再能像以前那样阔气地拿出大笔资金了。当她向她过去资助的那些“商业合作伙伴”寻求帮助时，才发现那些精明的商马早已将她曾经的慷慨视为理所当然，甚至有的还对她的资助量少而心存不满。

不过劳雷特此次前来，也提出了她的解决方案：劳雷特此前长期资助闪电天马队，其公司也为许多闪电天马队退役成员安排了工作。那个乘风，之前因为与云宝有过节而最终被踢出闪电天马队的长距离飞行记录保持者，就是在接受了劳雷特的资助后成长为了如今的娱乐行业富商。如果由劳雷特介绍，让乘风投资层云堡政府，乘风很有可能接受。只不过不同于劳雷特那样慷慨，层云堡可能需要为乘风提供一些更高收益的回报... 比方说，廷马克图水晶开采以及军火走私许可执照...

“我们对于和那些投机商交易，并不感到很舒服...” 喷火说。

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_23_o0]
“当然，其中不包括您，我只是说乘风。”

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_23_o1]
“但有时我们也不得不这样做。”

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_23_TOOLTIP]
§C乘风§!将获得廷马克图独家开采权。

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_23_TRIGGER_TOOLTIP]
§C乘风§!已经获得了廷马克图独家开采权，层云堡将不能再征收高额税赋。

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_24]
天使投资 · 后续

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_24_desc]
“和煦身旁的那个书呆子跟班？” 喷火摘下墨镜瞥了一眼劳雷特小姐，惊讶地一度想要吹响她的教官哨子。

在喷火拒绝了劳雷特提出的与乘风合作的方案后，金主名单上的下一个便是羽蝶 —— 现任帝国首席经济顾问、曾主导云中城自由贸易试验区项目的总指挥。虽然喷火对这位已经成为帝国高层的小马、和煦与花花短裤麾下最得力的经济干将仍然抱有警惕，但从帝国日益疯狂的经济政策来看：身处政治中心坎特洛特的羽蝶，其实早已经完全被文官集团和秘密警察架空，他的自由主义理论已被丢到一边。

劳雷特小姐说，自己昨天在坎特洛特与羽蝶交流时，他表达了想要辞职回到层云堡的意图。羽蝶希望重新实践自己的理论，继续那个被呆蹄领主打断的经济改革试验，而不受帝国官员干扰的自治领是最好的试验场。但与此同时，他也明白帝国中的贵族们并不希望看到这个试验成功，会尽他们所能阻挠羽蝶的计划。这迫使羽蝶不得不留在坎特洛特，紧紧抓住他本就所剩不多的那点首席顾问的权力。因此，劳雷特小姐提议，由羽蝶出资，帮助层云堡政府解决资金问题：条件是层云堡要接纳羽蝶的经济理论进行改革，让羽蝶打造一个成功的试验区展示给和煦女皇。

“所以，我们层云堡修建餐馆，最终只是为了让羽蝶能帮着那个和煦变得更富有？” 喷火反问道，她的声音中带着一丝讽刺。
“可是，羽蝶的理论一旦成功，不止会让和煦变得富有，整个帝国的经济都会受益。每一只小马，普通的小马们，这里面也包括你和我以及层云堡。” 劳雷特说。

“我还是表示怀疑，” 听着劳雷特有些异常热情地推荐，喷火不屑地带上了墨镜。

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_24_o0]
“但，有时我们也不得不这样做。”

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_24_o1]
“我宁愿选择乘风也不要帝国。”

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_24_TOOLTIP]
§R层云堡政府将不能再干预经济。§!

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_24_TRIGGER_TOOLTIP]
§R因为接受了与羽蝶的合作，层云堡政府将不能再干预经济。§!

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_26]
新员工 · 上

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_26_desc]
“梆！”

正当喷火听着破空和雾轨报告本月小餐馆的马芬产能时，喷火的办公室大门突然被一声巨响震开，闯进来的是全身红色的火药桶。一时间，破空还没反应过来，雾轨已经吓得躲到了椅子后，而喷火正下意识的将自己的翅膀伸进抽屉里想要拿出一把铳枪，却注意到火药桶虽然表情愤怒至极，但身上也没有带着武器。

“两个疯子！” 火药桶没好气地骂着。“闪尘和滚雷都发了大财！我却什么！都！没有！”
火药桶一边叫喊着，一边看到喷火办公室桌子上的餐盒，雾轨还没来得及张口阻拦，火药桶已经打开了餐盒，将里面的三明治一口气吞了下去，雾轨也只好缩回椅子后面，看着自己做给破空的午餐被火药桶白白吃掉。

火药桶加入“淘汰者”，从不是想闪尘和滚雷那样，追求极限与刺激，他只是想要多赚点门票钱，多买点好吃的。只不过，自从闪尘与滚雷入狱后，巡回表演停止，火药桶和一众“淘汰者”小弟们就失去了收入来源。火药桶原本也一心盼着两位领导早日出狱，可没想到当他开始打理帮派事务时，才发现自己的领导们竟然都有着他从来不知道的小金库 — 闪尘靠着军火贩买、滚雷靠着赌博和囤积廷马克图水晶，都赚的盆满钵满。“她们两个都发了大财！” 火药桶又一次咬牙切齿地说着。“哪怕是多买几个三明治也好啊！宁愿挥霍在危险器材、训练场地和飞行表演上，也不愿意多买几个三明治！”

破空、雾轨与喷火六目相对，都不知道该如何回应这位“叛逃”自敌方队伍的冲动者。一位“淘汰者”会仅仅因为一点分赃不均就举报自己的首领吗？雾轨偷偷地靠向喷火，用翅膀拽着喷火的衣服，用眼神向喷火传达她的怀疑。而喷火倒也与“淘汰者”打过不少交道，清楚火药桶确实是个没什么头脑的家伙。喷火示意破空拿出笔记本：不论火药桶什么动机，先把供词记下来再说。

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_26_o0]
“先和我们说说军火贩买和赌博？”

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_27]
新员工 · 下

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_27_desc]
“... 这还没完，去年她们突然和我说，‘淘汰者’打算做点大事情，” 火药桶继续吃着雾轨刚刚从外面带回来的三明治，嘴里塞满了，还依然控诉着，“我当时还以为她们是要去搞什么大型表演，结果她们说要开马芬工厂。我去给她们帮忙，做了两天马芬后，她们就把我给赶出来了！”
听到这里，雾轨忍不住笑了出来。从去年开始“淘汰者”就开始在生产纸杯蛋糕爆炸物了。将军火当做马芬食物售卖确实是一个好主意：不仅能骗过警察，甚至有时候还能骗到客户和“淘汰者”自己的员工 — 比如火药桶。

说到这里，火药桶突然一停顿。看见办公室内的图表，正是小餐馆的马芬生产统计图，他的眼睛一下子亮了起来。“好呀！原来你们抓她们俩就是想要抢过她们的马芬生意！我可听说了，你们垄断了云中城的订单！全部！马芬！订单！” 火药桶越说越激动，口中的蔬菜、面包与番茄渣子四处飞溅，雾轨只好再一次躲到了破空的身后。
“我给了你们这么多对手的信息，你们的计划也被我撞见了。这下小餐馆的马芬生意，是不是得分我一杯羹！？” 火药桶用着完全不像是请求的口吻请求着。

就这样，火药桶成为了层云堡小餐馆的新员工，破空成为了火药桶的新员工培训负责者，雾轨认真整理了火药桶的口供，喷火则准备张贴逮捕闪尘与滚雷的通缉令，每一只小马都有光明的未来。只不过 — 小餐馆的第一年没有收益，产品全都交给了云中城，所以员工们只能领着层云堡政府发放的微薄补贴这件事，喷火最终也没敢对火药桶说出口。

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_27_o0]
忍俊不禁

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_28]
谐律主义教育

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_28_desc]
层云堡餐馆的午后，火药桶正躺在角落里的长椅上打着呼噜，《友谊日记·注解版》打开着扣在他的身上，旁边还摆着似乎是一瓶红酒。

结束了中午的生意，与雾轨一起收拾好了后厨，破空走向了火药桶，用翅膀尖戳了戳他。被惊醒的红色飞马差点从长椅上滚下来。《友谊日记》也掉在地上，才翻到了第三页，里面夹着另外一本书，上面都是些扑克牌、魔术道具之类的内容。

“你往友谊教材里夹私货？” 破空挑起眉毛，用翅膀把书翻到扉页，《伟大而又全能的特丽克西教你20个生活中的魔术技巧》几个烫金字在阳光下闪闪发亮。 “你怎么还学起魔术来了？宁可学这个也不学友谊？”

睡眼惺忪的火药桶刚想要发脾气，却做了一次深呼吸，“才不是！让我读《友谊日记》不就是为了治我的暴脾气吗？我看《魔术技巧》控制情绪的方法更实用！”

破空看到没有发脾气的火药桶似乎也有些惊喜，但还是像一名真正的老师一样劝诫道：“也不全是，谐律的思想还包括许多其他的方面，比如宽容、理解、尊重、帮助朋友... 这些都是你需要学习的。” 破空看了看火药桶，看他有些不满但又没有发作的样子，也许是为了钱？还是他的脾气真的有所改善？

“道理我都懂，但是为什么要学这么旧的《友谊日记》，坎特洛特不是都发表了新版本的谐律思想了吗？为什么不学新的？” 火药桶正不耐烦地嘀咕着，看到破空的脸色越来越阴沉，他赶紧补充，“... 额... 我是说，你们让我学旧的那就学嘛，我又没说不学！倒是你，也该读读《魔术技巧》来控制一下你的脾气了！” 随后带着他的《友谊日记》、《魔术技巧》与红酒离开了餐馆，留下不知道说什么好的破空。

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_28_o0]
总之他有在学了

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_29]
模范学员

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_29_desc]
几个月过去，火药桶像是已经完全变成了另一只小马 — 就在今天中午，专心计算餐馆本月收支的雾轨飞行时不小心撞倒了火药桶，将他推到了一大桶马芬糖浆中。雾轨吓坏了，连连向满身裹着糖浆的火药桶道歉，但他却只是自己从桶中爬了出来，什么也没说便离开了。
火药桶不再是暴脾气了。餐馆的员工们惊讶地讨论着这一变化。破空正在准备为火药桶颁发模范学员奖牌；破空则将火药桶的变化报告给了喷火。“这是谐律主义教育成功的一次模板案例！” 破空在报告中这样写到。不过，破空的任务也并未完成：有员工反映火药桶并没怎么认真看那些谐律主义教材，最近的精神似乎也并不好，有些呆滞木讷，时常感到困倦。破空联想到之前与火药桶的交流中他每次总会带着一瓶红酒，不由得担心火药桶是否染上了酗酒的毛病，甚至有可能是接触了成瘾性的“天马快乐水”。
总之，火药桶的积极变化是有目共睹的，还差最后一个测试，这位模范学员就可以顺利毕业了 —— 他那唯利是图的毛病改好了么？接下来，喷火会假称因为第一年的马芬订单没有回报，因此没有火药桶的奖金，看看他的反应如何（实际上喷火与破空已经商量好了自掏腰包为火药桶准备了丰厚的奖金）。

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_29_o0]
有趣

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_30]
节俭的奢侈 · 上

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_30_desc]
天气工厂西部，一只镀着银镶着钻的小轿缓缓停下，后面跟着与其奢华完全不相称的只有两只小马的保镖团队。西装革履的羽蝶从小轿中走出，小心翼翼地。他与他的小轿一样，就像是一个自相矛盾的混合体：既奢华张扬，又内向收敛。
劳雷特小姐早已在此等候多时，很快便上前向帝国首席经济顾问羽蝶介绍起了周边的情况。当劳雷特小姐看到羽蝶的小轿时，她也很识趣地没有将其吹捧一番 — 因为劳雷特小姐清楚羽蝶其实非常讨厌这个小轿。平民出身的羽蝶看不惯坎特洛特那些贵族老爷和官僚们的骄奢淫逸，但若是不像他们一样纸醉金迷，就无法融入他们，导致他的一切经济政策和改革决议都推行不下去。因此，他不得不选择定制了一只尽可能看上去奢华，而又尽可能简小便宜的小轿。
此次考察天气工厂，羽蝶是趁着出访云中城的机会，脱离坎特洛特的命令秘密私自前来的。那些坎特洛特一个个肥头大耳的小马们只觊觎着云中城，想要让那些在呆蹄管理下貌似无穷无尽的马芬工厂转而为帝国生产奢侈品与武器。而只有羽蝶一只小马看清了云中城的真正价值：已经被遗弃的帝国气象局掌握着世界天气的控制权。只有让风之魔散去，整个小马利亚帝国才能获得长久的富裕，温暖的土地才能支撑得起女皇与那些腐败官僚的高额开支。而不同于云中城无法交流的呆蹄，羽蝶将希望寄托在相对独立于帝国政治环境，还没有被那些秘密警察渗透的层云堡政府上：羽蝶希望在层云堡自治区实践自己的经济学理念，以此向坎特洛特证明自己的价值，最终劝说女皇加大对气象局的投资，和对全国范围内的经济改革...

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_30_o0]
离开了帝国的管理，天气工厂自己似乎活得还不错

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_31]
节俭的奢侈 · 下

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_31_desc]
... 即使如今的羽蝶已经不再接触基层事务，羽蝶也从不会忘记当初他的当初的恐惧...
那还是塞拉斯蒂娅公主的时代，学习经济学的羽蝶以第一名的成绩从塞拉斯蒂娅皇家学院毕业，进入皇宫成为花花短裤麾下的一名实习生。但初入皇宫的第一项任务就差点终结了羽蝶的政治生涯：夏至庆典的物资调度工作做得一团糟。好在，在那最低谷的时期，和煦光流 — 那时还并未成为女皇的幼驹 — 发现了这位天才并安抚了他几近崩溃的情绪。随后在M6的帮助下，羽蝶有惊无险地度过了那一晚。
自那之后，羽蝶便深刻意识到一个道理：计划永远赶不上变化。没有小马有能力预知未来，即便是那位具有强迫症热爱制作计划表的暮光闪闪也不行。当他从“无为而治”的角度重新审视那些皇家学院旧贵族们的经济学理论时，他意识到了一个新的可能性：小马们具有自发组织经济活动的能力 — 就像一只小马开始唱歌，其他小马也会跟着唱歌一样。也许，小马们并不需要经济学家，并不需要他和花花短裤这样的官僚，甚至并不需要公主。只有将一切交还给小马们让他们自由地生产、销售与购买，羽蝶便再也无需回顾那一晚制定计划时的焦头烂额。
只不过，直到羽蝶的计划被摆在和煦光流女皇的书桌上的那一刻，羽蝶才意识到，那个在自己最绝望时帮助自己的友谊女皇，似乎也并不总是那么友善...

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_31_o0]
唉...

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_32]
秘密会议 · 上

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_32_desc]
当破空与雾轨推门进入喷火的办公室时，喷火正准备送别看起来愁容满面的劳雷特小姐。喷火安慰道，“劳雷特小姐，我们下次再商量。”
劳雷特小姐低着头出门时，恰好撞上了破空，将破空背上的背包撞落在地，文件撒了一地：里面是许多关于层云堡的文件，有的是关于餐馆的收支，有的是关于退役闪电天马的发展跟踪，有的标着大大的“绝密”字样... 而有的则是破空开小差时的涂鸦。或许是由于读了太多《友谊日记》，破空简陋的涂鸦上画着他佩戴着和谐之元，像曾经的暮光闪闪那样施展彩虹激光的样子。即使是刚刚还在愁容满面的劳雷特小姐，也没忍住笑了出来。破空则尴尬地赶紧挡住那些文件，说着什么“都是机密，不能看”之类的话。
雾轨则并没有笑，因为她清楚今天破空要与喷火讨论的议题有多么严肃 —— 也就是地上那些标着“绝密”的文件：破空已经计划了许久，打算趁着帝国忙于东方事务的时候，让层云堡宣布从帝国独立并高举谐律主义地旗帜向帝国发起挑战，与东方的朋友一起重振谐律的荣光。
作为前自由云中城运动参与者，自由层云堡运动领袖，层云堡自治领领长喷火自然懂得层云堡的渺小。面对帝国，层云堡的独立也许不过是一场自杀式的闹剧。但另一方面，看着新复原的闪电天马学院，喷火也不得不怀疑自己是否已经被过去的失败所束缚：看着破空与雾轨两张年轻的面孔，他们做到了自己多年来未能实现的事情。他们让闪电天马学院重新开张，让层云堡经济从依赖于帝国补贴变为餐饮业与水晶工业带动的自主经济...

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_32_o0]
也许，听听破空的计划也不是坏事...

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_33]
秘密会议 · 下

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_33_desc]
天气工厂，彩虹工厂，与闪电天马学院 —— 这三个地方有着数量最多的退役闪电天马在工作，如今这三个地区名义上分属名流谷、云中城与层云堡。破空提议，即使层云堡如今无法直面帝国，对付云中城与名流谷边界的民兵则是一件轻而易举的事情。如果层云堡可以通过突然袭击夺取这些地方，帝国得知后也将为时已晚。更别说帝国的军队都被牵制在东线，没有理由会派兵前来管这些辖区之间的内部矛盾。与此同时，层云堡也可以借机彻底铲除盘踞在独角山脉的“淘汰者”，稳固廷马克图的水晶矿区。
而后，破空继续建议道，层云堡控制了这三个地区，就真正有机会集结几乎所有曾经的闪电天马队成员，重建一支整个小马利亚无可匹敌的空中力量。闪电天马将重返天空！随后，破空与雾轨分别展示了一些详细的分析，对于帝国的军队部署，边境的民兵力量，以及坎特洛特的态度推演等... 他们也询问了层云堡其他方面的意见，乘风和商业委员会也表示强烈同意，愿意出资和招揽计划成员 —— 当然不是因为乘风的前闪电天马队员身份，而只是他希望能将廷马克图水晶工业的生意做到帝国的辖区去。
最终，这一计划被定名为“重返天空”计划，而闪电天马队将在近期开始集结以支撑这一计划的推进。

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_33_o0]
行动开始

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_34]
闪光蓝色马芬

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_34_desc]
层云堡食堂新品：闪光蓝色马芬！

§g“发光的是什么材料？确定能吃吗？”§!

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_34_o0]
好吧

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_35]
飞翔马芬

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_35_desc]
层云堡食堂新品：飞翔马芬！

§g“是的，翅膀确实好吃。”§!

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_35_o0]
好吧

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_36]
奢华黑马芬

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_36_desc]
层云堡食堂新品：奢华黑马芬！

§g“额... 这确定不是烤糊了吗？”§!

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_36_o0]
好吧

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_37]
水晶马芬

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_37_desc]
层云堡食堂新品：水晶马芬！

§g“不是怎么还没完没了了？这能吃吗？”§!

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_37_o0]
好吧

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_38]
苹果派

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_38_desc]
层云堡食堂新品：苹果派！

§g“听说是有小马实在受不了一天天只吃马芬了，于是自掏腰包买了苹果派的食材交给了餐馆...”§!

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_38_o0]
好吧

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_39]
重返天空

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_39_desc]
当重组后的闪电天马掠过层云堡的天际线时，整座城市屏住了呼吸。黄蓝相间的身影撕裂云层，尾迹在夕阳下拖曳出流光的弧线 —— 仿佛谐律精华从未破碎，仿佛战争从未发生。
领队的飞火昂起头，翅膀的每一次拍打都精准如钟表。她身后，雾轨和破空以完美的编队紧随，气流在他们蹄下编织成无形的阶梯。
“就是现在！” 当编队继续向前飞行即将抵达坎特洛特时，飞火长嘶一声。三匹飞马同时加速，云层在激波中坍缩，蒸发，最终——

轰！
彩虹音爆在坎特洛特上空炸开，半径是云宝黛西当年纪录的三倍。七彩的涟漪扫过大地，风之魔的残影尖叫着消散，被奴役的小马们突然停下了工作。他们的鬃毛无风自动，眼中亮起陌生的金光。
传单如雪片般落下。
贵族用颤抖的蹄子拾起一张。
秘密警察的枪掉在了地上。
皇宫的露台上，和煦光流揉碎纸页，却听见自己的声音在不受控制地高喊：
“控制台是魔法！”

——接着，世界卡顿了。
天空像故障的屏幕般闪烁，飞火的翅膀突然定格在俯冲姿态，破空的笑容凝固成像素化的马赛克。天边传来雾轨轻轻的叹息声：“...连控制台都觉得这太荒谬了。”

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_39_o0]
全剧终

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_40]
天亮请睁眼

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_40_desc]
今天是层云堡的大日子。才刚刚清晨，太阳的光芒甚至还没能浮现到云层之上时，在刚有微光的层云堡市政府会议室内就已经挤满了天马们：谐律主义学徒与层云堡餐饮集团创始者破空，层云堡政府顾问兼萼叶民兵领袖雾轨，云中城商业委员会主席乘风，还有一众前闪电天马队成员或学员们，齐聚一堂。
破空早已将演讲稿准备好，还特地检查了三四遍这次的演讲稿反面没有自己的涂鸦；雾轨则面无表情地坐在一旁，一会儿看着破空，一会儿又看看窗外的风景，没有小马知道她在想什么。乘风则是坐在桌边，手里拿着一杯星璇咖啡自顾自地喝着...
...
当第一缕阳光终于透过云层的缝隙从下方射来，将会议室的天花板染成橙红色时，破空已经第五次展开演讲稿，薄云纸边缘已被汗水洇出波浪纹。雾轨忽然起身走到窗边，云玻璃映出她瞳孔里跳动的微光 —— 东方云层开始渗出铁锈色。
市政府外的云层上，闪电天马队的一批年轻面孔正全副武装，穿着红蓝相间的制服随时准备起飞，但也因这漫长的等待而显得有些不安。乘风用汤匙拨弄着咖啡杯底部残留的咖啡渍，似乎想从中看出些什么，又放弃了，打了个哈欠。当乘风放下汤匙的时候，整个会议室里就只剩下了破空反复折叠演讲稿的声音。
...
当白得发亮的阳光终于彻底穿透了云层之时，会议室的大门才被打开，走进来的却并非喷火而是一位满脸惊恐的萼叶民兵。
“是帝国打过来了吗？” 乘风见状立即丢掉了咖啡杯上前询问，一副马上就要冲出会议室离开层云堡的样子；破空猛地抬起头丢掉了稿子，雾轨也猛地从窗边转身。
“是... 喷火领长... 在餐馆后面的苹果摊...” 萼叶民兵翅膀上融化的冰晶混着血迹滴落，“我们发现她倒在那里... 身上全都是血...”

太阳终于升到了云层之上，血红色的朝阳完整地出现在了窗外，朝阳如目光般直直地从盯着会议室。

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_40_o0]
什么？！

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_41]
层云堡枪击案

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_41_desc]
层云堡枪击案让这个没什么存在感的小镇终于罕见地登上了一次新闻头条：昨夜，层云堡自治领领长在层云堡餐馆遭到不明身份小马的枪击，现已经被送往层云堡医院进行急救，暂未脱离生命危险。
帝国女皇和煦光流第一时间对此事表示了关切，强烈谴责了刺杀一名帝国自治领公职小马的行为，并表示将会排除秩序部与友谊部协助层云堡政府调查此案。担任代理领长破空，喷火的学徒，拒绝了帝国的此次协助，表示层云堡会独立调查此案。

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_41_o0]
好吧

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_41_o1]
搞不好就是帝国干的

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_42]
枪声之后

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_42_desc]
没过多久，层云堡警方就通过现场的痕迹锁定了罪犯：在喷火遇刺的苹果派摊发现了被遗弃的铳枪、血迹、一些玻璃瓶的碎片和一滩似乎溶入一些血液的粉红色的水。铳枪属于喷火自己，但这破碎的玻璃瓶不属于喷火，貌似是 —— 破空立即想起了这是火药桶的瓶子。
那些残余的粉红色液体立马被送去检查，而破空也立即在全层云堡发布了对火药桶的通缉令。但令破空想不明白的是，为什么？
是谐律主义教育没有做到位？还是火药桶的一时冲动？还是火药桶真的有酗酒甚至滥用“天马快乐水”的问题？还是说... 难道从最开始他就是“淘汰者”派来的卧底？

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_42_o0]
好吧

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_43]
登顶层云

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_43_desc]
本身的“重返天空”计划被打乱，原本要对帝国举起反抗旗帜的行动在失去喷火的领导后被一拖再拖。这让成为了代理领长的破空极为不满，他心心念念的《友谊日记》读后实践环节就这样在一场似乎可能就来自帝国和帝国相关势力策划的肮脏刺杀中被打断了。
正因如此，本就积极主张推广谐律主义的破空在成为代理领长后没给帝国什么好脸色。尽管雾轨一再提醒破空认清层云堡的地位，但破空不仅在刺杀案调查一事上公开拒绝了女皇的协助，还以调查为由停止参加了此前喷火都要参加的与坎特洛特官员的“友谊交流活动”。
很快，坎特洛特那边就传来了花花短裤的信：“帝国忠诚的领长喷火遭遇不测，女皇日夜难眠，辗转反侧，担忧层云堡的居民们的安危，建议层云堡立即举行领长补缺选举，选出新的领长来安抚民心。”花花短裤在信中说到，帝国向来支持层云堡自治领的自主权，帝国会尊重层云堡居民的选择。而在信的后面又附上了一份的具体的提案，其中包括：坎特洛特希望层云堡能在4个月内完成选举工作、建议代理领长避嫌、防范执政党利用职务之便为选举造势和压制选民。最后，花花短裤罗列了一些帝国推荐的候选者：“淘汰者”闪尘、气象局局长羽蝶、劳雷特·多芙小姐、以及后面几十位坎特洛特的官员名。
破空坐在喷火的领长办公室，听雾轨朗读完帝国的两封文件，气得重重锤了一蹄桌子，差点将之前刚刚补好的凹痕又砸了出来。

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_43_o0]
这就是帝国所谓的“自主权”吗？

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_43_TOOLTIP]
解锁系列§R限时§!决议：§Y枪声之后§!。

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_44]
火药桶的口供

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_44_desc]
破空和雾轨亲自赶到了警局，投过那薄薄的云层覆盖着的单向玻璃窗，他们看到了坐在审讯室内的火药桶。火药桶不再像曾经那样张扬易怒，也不知是因为犯了错的愧疚，还是因为谐律主义教育的“成功”，如今的火药桶已经变得沉默寡言，甚至有些畏缩。
还没等破空张口，火药桶已经主动开口：“是... 是我干的... 我真不是故意的... 我也不知道怎么回事——” 眼见火药桶开始要推脱责任，破空立刻一拍桌子：“不知道？是不是闪尘派你来卧底的？” 破空此刻只需要一个名字，只要能够证明火药桶与闪尘依然有着联系，就可以主动出击剿灭淘汰者这股反谐律势力了。又或者，如果火药桶是受到了帝国的指使... 那“重返天空”计划就可以再一次被提上日程。
雾轨见状，从包中拿出之前案发现场玻璃瓶的碎片，递给了破空。破空将其展示给了火药桶，严厉地质问：“你说，这是什么？！”
火药桶看了看玻璃瓶，看了看瞪着他的破空，再看了看眼神中满是失望的雾轨，一时无言以对。雾轨与破空此时就成了好警察-坏警察的经典组合，雾轨走上前去轻轻地拍了拍火药桶的背，“放松。之前玻璃瓶里装的，是‘天马快乐水’吗？如果是的话不要害怕，我们会帮你通过药物治疗这个问题的。”
火药桶看看雾轨，没有敢说话。破空却也不希望这件事从敌对势力策划的暗杀，变成一个“天马快乐水”成瘾的小马的悲剧，于是继续追问：“如果你能说出这瓶子里的‘天马快乐水’是怎么来的，我们就放过你。是不是帝国给你的？还是闪尘给你的？选一个吧！”
“我... 我是从帝国那边拿的！” 火药桶犹豫着说了出来，破空立刻将其记在笔记上。而雾轨却看着火药桶感到困惑，似乎是非常不理解火药桶为什么会和帝国有联系。“你说的是真话吗？” 雾轨继续拍着火药桶的背，用温柔的语气问道。

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_44_o0]
“...”

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_45]
廷马克图富商

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_45_desc]
在水晶工业彻底放开后不久，乘风和他的商业委员会下的注册商马们就很快垄断了廷马克图水晶的开采、加工与销售。云中城商业委员会摇身一变几乎成了廷马克图商业委员会。
但商马的欲望从不会停止与在一个行业实现垄断，商业委员会的成员们开始讲视角看向层云堡及其周边地区的各个行业：层云堡的餐饮生意、淘汰者的军火生意、彩虹工厂的“天马快乐水”、天气工厂的供暖行业... 他们全都要。
这便是乘风所索取的专营权的真正影响和最终结果，一个足以靠资金实力干预廷马克图地区，乃至整个层云堡的庞然巨物。除经济影响外，乘风还在积极寻求政治影响力，过分热情地尝试与层云堡政府合作、参与到政府的每一项行动中来...

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_45_o0]
看他们能疯狂多久

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_46]
廷马克图富商

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_46_desc]
在水晶工业彻底放开后不久，乘风和他的商业委员会下的注册商马们就很快垄断了廷马克图水晶的开采、加工与销售。云中城商业委员会摇身一变几乎成了廷马克图商业委员会。
但商马的欲望从不会停止与在一个行业实现垄断，商业委员会的成员们开始讲视角看向层云堡及其周边地区的各个行业：层云堡的餐饮生意、淘汰者的军火生意、彩虹工厂的“天马快乐水”、天气工厂的供暖行业... 他们全都要。
这便是羽蝶的“自由贸易”所没能预料到的后果 —— 不加限制的竞争总是导致一个通吃的赢者。如今的乘风不仅几乎独享了羽蝶改革的全部收益，更是准备将天气工厂也兼并到商业委员会中。也难怪羽蝶的改革没能在帝国推行成功 —— 就帝国的那些盘根错节的利益关系来说，羽蝶的“自由贸易”不过是那些秘密警察和贵族官僚们敛财的新途径罢了。虽然和煦光流拒绝羽蝶的提议也许是出于私利，但这倒是阴差阳错避免了一场悲剧。

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_46_o0]
看他们能疯狂多久

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_47]
雾轨的小纸条

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_47_desc]
“喷火领长，抱歉我欺骗了您...”
“关于此前在会议上讨论的‘重返天空’计划，其实我并没有很强的信心。经过对坎特洛特官员的态度分析以及帝国当前空闲军力的评估，我们认为帝国并不会坐视不理，反而会加大对层云堡的干预力度。经过对军力的评估，即使是我们最引以为豪的空军，也将完全没有机会与帝国抗衡。”
“我之所以隐瞒这些，只是为了不想让破空太过失望。他读了太多《友谊日记》，每天都在思考这些，我曾经想让他冷静分析一下，但最后都不欢而散。”
“所以，我恳求您：为了层云堡，请不要进行‘重返天空’计划。为了破空，请不要戳穿我的谎言。我可以为您提供一个拒绝实行计划的借口，而这个借口绝非另一个谎言，而是千真万确的隐患：”
“警惕乘风！我们之前提到计划本身已经获得了乘风的热情支持，但经过背景调查，我发现乘风的商业委员会所从事的军火生意，并非曾经我们设想的那样独立或者与闪尘有竞争关系 —— 闪尘就是乘风的主要供货商之一。”
“这意味着我们的‘重返天空’计划中关于剿灭‘淘汰者’的部分，很可能已经被乘风泄露给了‘淘汰者’，而闪尘她们又很可能进一步将整个计划泄露给了帝国...”
“当然，我理解行动已经开始难以直接中止。但我还是希望可以和您继续讨论一下此事。”

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_47_o0]
好吧

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_48]
飞入飓风

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_48_desc]
“首先，我们要在此为仍在昏迷中的喷火送去祝福。” 闪尘清了清嗓子，对着观众们讲道。在独角山脉靠近云中城一侧，“淘汰者”正在组织新一次演出 — 自闪尘宣布参与层云堡补缺选举以来的第一次。虽说他们的演出曾经只有少数叛逆幼驹或者非主流飞马喜欢，这一次却坐满了西装革履的天马政客，显然这已经不止是一次演出了。也正因如此，即使是谁都知道闪尘与喷火关系不和，但在这个时候闪尘还是不得不为喷火美言了几句。
“喷火的遭遇是不幸的，但我们必须继续前进。层云堡的补缺选举，既是一次考验，也是一次机会。是属于我们天马的机会...”
随后，闪尘讲起了天马古城 — 廷马克图，这里曾是天马们的骄傲，却在虫茧女王的进攻下毁灭。闪尘将其归咎于安逸：那些水晶生意带来的富庶让曾经在云层中翱翔的天马们忘记了自己的使命，收起翅膀在城邦中生活了下来，在一代代的安逸中失去了飞翔的勇气。而闪尘 — 自称是廷马克图的遗嗣 — 不愿看到千年后的天马们再重复历史的悲剧。随后，闪尘预告了其竞选纲领的最主要项目：飓风计划。
闪尘计划整合整个层云堡与云中城，建立一个专属于天马们的巨大的“飞行训练营”，她称呼为新廷马克图。在那里，决定天马们生活的将只有飞行的速度与高度，而不是财富的数量或是官职的高低；在那里，天马们将在飞翔中获得一切，而不是在地面上、在风之魔的阴影中苟且偷生；在那里，天马们将用自己创造的“飓风”守卫自己的家园。具体地，闪尘拿出了天气实验室曾经的若干科研提案：通过飓风发电的研究、通过飓风驱散风之魔的研究、飓风的军事化研究、飓风与天马飞行能力的结合研究...
“... 我们决定飞入飓风。我们决定在几年内飞入飓风，并实现更多梦想。并非它们轻而易举，而正是因为它们困难重重。因为这个目标将促进我们实现最佳的组织并测试我们顶尖的技术和力量，因为这个挑战我们乐于接受，因为这个挑战我们不愿推迟，因为这个挑战我们志在必得，其他的挑战也是如此。”

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_48_o0]
好吧

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_48_TOOLTIP]
解锁§Y枪声之后§!中的§R限时§!决议：§Y阻止淘汰者巡回演出§!

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_49]
雾轨的分析 · 上

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_49_desc]
就在破空即将依据火药桶的口供重启对帝国的宣战计划时，雾轨拉住了他：“破空，你仔细想一想。”
看着一脸疑惑的破空，雾轨叹了口气：“之前都说过多少次了，让你少读一些《友谊日记》，多读一读和煦光流和坎特洛特的那些书。他们的思想虽然不正确，但他们的政治智慧显然比那暮光公主那童话般的故事对我们生存有帮助得多——”
破空的脸色立即阴沉下来，非常没好气地看着雾轨。“你到底想说什么？”
雾轨见状也识趣地立即停止了对暮光公主著作的妄言，转而重新拿起火药桶的口供：“如果火药桶真的是帝国派来的，为什么他没有在当晚就逃回帝国，而是在第二天前来自首？帝国又怎么会允许？”
破空张口想要反驳，却一时语塞，也沉思起来。见状，雾轨继续慢慢说道：“我认为，火药桶更有可能是‘淘汰者’派来的，刺杀喷火，然后嫁祸帝国，目的就是让我们与帝国起冲突。乘风不是我们的盟友，他很可能已经将计划泄露给了‘淘汰者’，从而给了‘淘汰者’一个机会。”
破空听完后的疑问不减反增：“淘汰者？闪尘不是和帝国一伙的吗？而且我们本就要和帝国开战，为什么还要多此一举？”
雾轨摇了摇头，叹了口气。

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_49_o0]
“你还是没明白”

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_50]
雾轨的分析 · 下

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_50_desc]
“滚雷曾经当过帝国的走狗，但是闪尘从来没有。闪尘就是个疯子，既不和我们一伙，也不和帝国一伙。剿灭‘淘汰者’也曾是‘重返天空’计划的一部分，而现在，层云堡进入大选，如果闪尘能借机加入到计划中来，既能避免争端，又能审时度势两面下注。” 雾轨一点也不急躁，依然慢慢地为蒙在鼓里的破空解释道。
“所以... 你是建议我们在对帝国宣战前，先剿灭‘淘汰者’？” 破空问道。
“也不行，闪尘已经第一时间宣布参与了层云堡补缺选举。如果对她采取军事行动，看上去就像是我们要迫害政治竞争者一样。虽然层云堡民众都支持我们，但这会给帝国一个理由。”
“那这不正好对帝国——” 破空刚想要打断雾轨，却被雾轨再次打断。雾轨以破空几乎完全看不见的幅度翻了一个白眼，继续说下去：
“我们只能先将火药桶的罪行与他和‘淘汰者’的联系通过小道消息公之于众，营造舆论，赢下补缺选举 — 我们一定能赢的，这没什么悬念 — 然后再清算闪尘，最后再通过滚雷供出帝国。路要一步步走，云要一片片飞，破空。”

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_50_o0]
也许破空听懂了...吧？

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_51]
萼叶档案：乘风

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_51_desc]
雾轨从萼叶获得的情报表明，乘风正在两头下注：一方面，他在公开场合支持破空与现任层云堡政府；另一方面，他也帮着介绍了许多委员会成员前去参加闪尘的表演与晚宴...
对于一位商马来说，这种行为十分正常，毕竟他们唯一在乎的就是最大化收益最小化风险。但乘风的行为是否会代表更多群体的态度？我们那虚高的支持率是否有可能只是一群墙头草在填充？
值得密切关注乘风的后续动向，以及云中城商业委员会中的主流态度。同时也要注意反侦察，若乘风意识到层云堡当局正在监视竞争对手与他们的支持者，这种舆论影响可能是我们无法承受的。

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_51_o0]
好吧

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_52]
萼叶档案：刺杀案嫌疑犯

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_52_desc]
经过一个月，雾轨终于将萼叶组织的调查结果汇总成了报告交给了破空，然而在报告内，却难以下定任何结论：没有小马可以被逃脱怀疑。
嫌疑最大的当属闪尘 — 火药桶本就是“淘汰者”的成员、闪尘的下属，在喷火遇刺后闪尘又第一时间准备好了竞选纲领与演讲，这些都让她成为了最有嫌疑的对象。
接着是乘风 — 谁都知道这是个贪婪而不择手段的商马，虽然他得到了他想要的一切，但总是想要更多。喷火之前就曾表达过限制商业委员会的垄断的想法，可能因此成为了乘风想要除掉的对象。
再是名流谷 — 夺取彩虹工厂是“重返天空”计划的一部分，他们可能从商业委员会那里听到了风声，想要先行一步 — 毕竟火药桶的失态很可能就来自于“天马快乐水”，而那是名流谷彩虹工厂的产品。
然后是羽蝶 — 帝国派往层云堡的官员，因其收购天气工厂的打算与喷火存在利益冲突，也自然有可能因此雇凶作案。更进一步，他的背后可能是花花短裤的势力。
即使是温柔善良的劳雷特·多芙小姐也不能排除嫌疑 — 多芙家族在层云堡的生意一直不温不火，最近在尝试进军水晶工业和彩虹工厂，但都比竞争者晚了一步。在之前的秘密会议前，破空与雾轨曾经看到她与喷火似乎进行了一场不太愉快的交流。也正是那次照面，她撞倒了破空，看到了关于“重返天空”计划的秘密文件。事实上，根据层云堡市政厅的记录，喷火遇刺前最后一个会面的对象就是劳雷特小姐。
总而言之，这份报告没能给出任何结论，反而让整个层云堡的各方势力都成为了被怀疑的对象。更有甚者，闪尘也在散布谣言，称喷火遇刺是破空与雾轨的夺权阴谋，想要借此机会将他们俩也拉下水。

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_52_o0]
扑朔迷离

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_53]
贵客

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_53_desc]
当水晶行业的蛋糕被瓜分得差不多的时候，乘风盯上了下一个机会 — 新成立的气象局，和其下属的天气工厂与新天气实验室。
当乘风踏入喷火的办公室时，喷火已经泡好了冒着热气的星璇咖啡，等着他了。乘风做下，刚喝了一口咖啡，还没等他咽下，喷火就抢先开了口：“天气工厂，算了吧。我打算交给羽蝶了。”
乘风差点要讲咖啡喷出来，猛地坐直，被咖啡呛了几口，咳嗽了几声，才缓过来劲。趁此机会，喷火不给乘风回话的时间，赶紧继续说：“我不信任帝国的官员。但是帝国在层云堡不会作威作福太久了，所以我打算把天气工厂划给羽蝶，到时候我们就能找个借口收归层云堡政府了。今天上午我已经和羽蝶谈过了。这事和你没什么关系，我们也不希望到时候收归政府的时候，坐在桌子那头的是你。没有什么个马恩怨，只是生意，希望你能理解。”
乘风愣了几秒，刚想要张口，再次被喷火打断：“不过我邀请你来当然不是因为这个原因。而是彩虹工厂，我希望你能劝说一下劳雷特小姐...”

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_53_o0]
各司其职

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_54]
贵客

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_54_desc]
羽蝶已经来到层云堡一段时间了，但这还是第一次，他见到了层云堡自治领领长喷火。
羽蝶文质彬彬地做到了喷火的办公桌前，看了看面前冒着热气的星璇咖啡，将其推到了一边。他看了喷火一眼，便开始解释他的提案，“自从层云堡实施自由贸易以来，经济增长...”
喷火眼看着羽蝶拿出一份份数据，表格，折线图，饼图... 差点想要打个哈欠。她用翅膀轻轻敲打着桌面，心里想着：真是个无趣的家伙。
“... 如果我们气象局宣布对天气工厂进行市场化改革，预计在几个月内，我们就可以——”
喷火终于忍不住了，打断了羽蝶的长篇大论：“乘风。我打算把天气工厂交给乘风，今天下午我就要和他也谈一谈。毕竟我们都知道，你私有化后，最终还是会被委员会买下的。”
羽蝶愣了几秒，继续说道：“确实，商业委员会的垄断行为值得我们关注。但我相信，随着市场自发的调节，通过引入外部竞争者，我们可以打破——”
喷火又一次打断了他：“不是这个意思，“我邀请你来当然不是因为这个原因。而是彩虹工厂，我希望你能劝说一下劳雷特小姐...”

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_54_o0]
各司其职

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_55]
雾轨的小纸条

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_55_desc]
“喷火领长，关于天气工厂，我按照您的要求进行了调查。”
“简而言之，我认为天气工厂既不适合交给羽蝶也不适合交给乘风。这里的工会有着很强的独立性和团结性，正如层云堡一样。天气工厂是一个有着反叛精神的地区，无论是那些大资本还是帝国的官僚都从未能驯服过这片地方，我也不认为羽蝶和乘风会是特例。不过，我建议您可以让他们互相竞争，告诉羽蝶会将天气工厂交给乘风，告诉乘风会将天气工厂交给羽蝶。然后我们看看他们的开价。”
“最终，天气工厂必然还是实际交由工会管理，而我们需要提前开始与工会接洽。一个可能的路径是，如果乘风获得胜利，我们可以以反垄断的名义直接代表政府公开与工会合作扳倒乘风。而如果羽蝶获得胜利，我们可以用反对帝国的名义暗中拉拢工会，架空羽蝶。”
“当然，这些都是我的一点微不足道的看法。我知道您会做出更好的选择。”

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_55_o0]
好吧

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_56]
新独角兽 · II

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_56_desc]
...滋滋... (TV噪音)
“——我们正在见证又一个独角兽的诞生！当然，这里并不是在说，又一只长着角会使用魔法的小马出生了，而是一家冉冉升起的新兴独角兽企业！” 现场记者兴奋地说道。
星璇咖啡，一个仅在近期才兴起的小家族咖啡厅，面向高端市场推出的高价格高质量咖啡，获得了商业委员会的多位慧眼如炬的会员的青睐。为了探究星璇咖啡爆火的原因，我们采访了小咖啡厅的老板娘。
“我们的秘诀？哦只不过是独角兽的眼泪和月光烘焙的咖啡豆。更主要的是 —— **独特性**！当劳雷特小姐说我们的拿铁‘喝起来像是和谐的回忆’时，我们就知道我们成功了。然后不知怎么的，层云堡政府听说了这件事。现在他们在招待所有贵宾时都用我们的咖啡，劳雷特小姐、羽蝶、还有乘风——他现在不仅是我们的顾客，还是我们最大的股东。它不只是一杯咖啡 —— 它是一种**生活方式**。” 星璇咖啡的老板娘眨了眨眼，她说的没错！这种在层云堡政府招待贵宾时的不成文规则，立刻在层云堡乃至大云城一带风靡开来。
然而，并不是所有的顾客都是咖啡爱好者，他们只是想要成为潮流的一部分。“在未来，所有的小马都将引用他们的水果！” 星璇咖啡的第二大股东恒星耀斑如是说，她向星璇咖啡的老板娘提议在菜单上添加来自名流谷的果汁。
“总之,” 现场记者总结道，“随着星璇咖啡计划上市，投资者们都在期待着分析师所称的‘第一家基于咖啡因的庞氏骗局’的股票。同时，我们其余的小马们也会在这里，花掉我们一周的薪水买一杯咖啡，只为拍张照片上传到云。画面交回演播室。”

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_56_o0]
好吧

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_57]
新独角兽 · I

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_57_desc]
...滋滋... (TV噪音)
“——我们正在见证又一个独角兽的诞生！当然，这里并不是在说，又一只长着角会使用魔法的小马出生了，而是一家冉冉升起的新兴独角兽企业！” 现场记者兴奋地说道。
廷马克图淘晶者协会，云中城商业委员会的下属组织，在一年内因廷马克图水晶首饰的爆火而忽然成为各个投资商的焦点：如果说曾经坎特洛特的贵族连层云堡和廷马克图的名字都没听说过，那么现在谁如果不能第一眼在地图上找出这一小马利亚最受欢迎水晶的产地，谁就基本可以告别商业顾问生涯了。
“淘晶者协会的前身是劳雷特小姐赞助的工马工会。” 乘风在接受采访时这样说道：“劳雷特小姐是一位非常善良和具有远见的小马，也是她当年为我提供了第一桶金。只可惜，她的商业头脑还有待提高。由于工会长期无偿提供法律援助，入不敷出，最终我与劳雷特小姐商议，愿意收购工会并承担其所有债务。”
“我最快意识到廷马克图水晶生意的前景，你们知道的，我永远是最快的。在闪电天马队的时候是，现在经商的时候也是。” 乘风说着，对自己感到十分满意。“于是我让工会的工马成员们都从天气工厂迁去廷马克图淘金，呃... 淘水晶，更准确地说。这样他们就可以用水晶当做报酬支付给工会，以获得工会的法律援助了。”
然而，并不是所有的关注者都赞同淘晶者协会的做法。
“工会的作用本就是组织工马与垄断企业谈判，如今却成为了垄断企业的一部分。我担心这会在工马中，尤其是那些拒绝搬家的天气工厂工马中，引起不满。” 也许是因为错过了这次财富机遇，劳雷特小姐略有不快地评价。
“淘晶者协会正在垄断廷马克图的采矿业，这是不健康的。” 帝国首席经济顾问羽蝶这样评价道：“比如说，就像坎特洛特一样。如今的坎特洛特化妆行业被鸢尾花的企业垄断，初期这带来了大量的就业和税收，但很快垄断就让帝国的经济一蹶不振——“
“哔——” 毫无征兆地，直播被坎特洛特掐断了。

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_57_o0]
好吧

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_58]
iHorn: 魔法，但没那么魔法。

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_58_desc]
§g（简约的说唱节奏，重低音）§!
你是陆马，你吃草，你种苹果。
你是飞马，你会飞，你搬云朵。
你很好，你很棒，但内心深处，总觉得缺少了什么。

隆重推出 iHorn。
§g（说唱：魔法，魔法，魔法，魔法。）§!
§g（展示光滑的反光铝合金外壳）§!
微微一亮。§g（不同种族的小马围着篝火跳舞）§!
轻轻一推。§g（飞马在高空中，用魔法拨开云朵）§!
缓缓一触。§g（陆马用魔法让书本悬浮）§!
移动那根胡萝卜。打开那扇门。点亮那根蜡烛。
“我曾经没有魔法，现在我连接 iMagic，享受iFriendship。”

§g（说唱：魔法，魔法，魔法，魔法。）§!
隐私。内置的。
由幻形灵测试，隐身大师。
舒适。轻量的。
由蹄博士认证，马体工学专家。
充电。无线的。
像提雷克一样，从空气中吸取能量。
最重要的是：

款式当然要有暮光紫色与和煦粉色。
§g（展示 iHorn Pro 和 iHorn Max）§!

§g（说唱：魔法，魔法，魔法，魔法。这是今年夏天最大的角。）§!
iHorn。魔法，但没那么魔法。


§g（本产品由小马谷、云中城和洛马基共同投资开发，并在蹄博士的技术领导下构思而成。产品测试阶段已在层云堡成功纳入高空适应性验证，并在云中城通过了严格的气象兼容性测试。本产品的理论框架和基础设计灵感整合了小马谷的传统魔法技术和源自风暴王岛的当代创新。iHorn 所实现的魔法能力会因购买者的小马种族分类、固有的个体生理差异以及对适用的地方法律法规的遵守情况而有所不同。特此明确指出，并非所有地区都支持所有宣传的魔法功能。强烈建议用户在部署前查阅现行的地方法律魔法使用规定。本设备明确设计旨在促进不同小马种群之间的文化交流和相互理解，严格遵守中立原则，不参与任何地区政治事务，包括但不限于帝国与抵抗力量之间的管辖权冲突，以及幻形灵和斑马之间的种族间分歧。我们坚持反对一切形式的交战和冲突的机构承诺。宣传材料中所描绘的多元、多民族和谐场景仅旨在说明产品的包容性设计理念。所有操作魔法能量均通过集成魔法核心和补充外部充电机制提供。无线充电功能的激活需要放置在专门指定的魔法能量传输场内。iHorn 包含精密魔法组件，因此不适合在以过度潮湿、颗粒物污染（例如泥浆）或极端气象事件为特征的环境中持续运行。必须严格避免直接暴露于强魔法干扰源，例如暗石。所有视觉媒体制作均坚持排他性地使用可持续采购的可再生材料，确保没有有情或无情的生物遭受伤害。本文件和产品规格的最终解释权完全归蹄博士实验室所有。© 蹄博士实验室。保留所有权利。所有有关法律或知识产权事宜的咨询，请致函洛马基财团的法律部门。雇佣幼驹生产iHorn的说法为不实谣言，洛马基财团保留追究法律责任的权利。）§!

[zh.EVENT_C04_MAIN_58_o0]
？

[zh.PIHC_IHORN]
iHorn
